forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 04-27-2017, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T19:25:48-07:00","id":1084824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084659#post1084659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this seems like as good an opportunity as any to talk about something that's been on my mind. I don't know about elsewhere in the world, but here in the US, it seems we are in an awkward position thanks to racism being seen as a Special Kind of Evil. Granted, racially-based predjdice is not a good thing, but we kind of have a tendency to equate &quot;racist&quot; = &quot;irredeemable monster&quot;. Which makes it very difficult to call people out on minor things related to race. You can't say &quot;hey, that joke you made kind of crossed a line for me&quot; without the other person lashing out defensively because how dare you accuse them of being &quot;a racist&quot;. The concept of micro-aggressions isn't taken seriously because the idea that such minor things could make someone &quot;a racist&quot; seems inane. When really the point is that you don't have to be &quot;a racist&quot; to engage in racially insensitive behavior, and that doesn't make you a horrible person, but we would all do well to be mindful of those things and to make an effort to address them.<br /> <br /> I feel like Avenue Q had the right idea and took the wrong lesson from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I've noticed as well. Its difficult to explain the concept of institutional racism and individual prejudice because we've created this image of a capital-R &quot;Racist&quot; with a Klan robe and a Nazi armband. A cartoon villain synonymous with evil. People think &quot;I can't be saying/doing something racist because that would make me a Racist and Racists Are Bad People. I'm not a bad person.&quot; We don't like shades of gray, we don't like self-reflection, and we like difficult solutions least of all. Its much easier to see the world as good people versus bad people, as opposed to a messy system of well-meaning people with prejudices they may not even be aware of that come out of cultural and historical baggage all making choices based on seemingly reasonable calculations and value judgments the aggregate of which still creates outcomes that are prejudicial and oppressive. <br /> <br /> I've grown to hate the Avenue Q song. Not because of itself, but because of the meme its turned into. &quot;Everybody's a little bit racist... therefore whatever it is I'm doing that's perceived as racist doesn't really matter and whoever is complaining about it is a hypocrite.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T20:13:10-07:00","id":1084831,"title":"","content":"its very interesting to me when I see people in gaming communities hold these types of conversations regarding race. Naturally, given the large number of white men who make up the table table top gaming genre, there are a lot of people like some on here (i won't name them specifically because i don't want to get banned and i have a feeling that mentioning people who are in their current situation might be a forum etiquette faux pa) who are so lost in their self supporting worldview that they have become convinced that white men are the real ones who are being persecuted by being expected to treat others as human beings for a change, and as many people have pointed out, they tend to sound like members of alt-right groups.<br /> <br /> then there are others who skirt the lines of apologist language, who don't agree with the alt-right sounding individuals, but want to make allowances for them, in politics they are often referred to as liberals, the moderates in the political spectrum who believe they are on the left simply because they are contrasted by the right.<br /> <br /> I am a person of color and a gamer, and i can tell you that this is not always the easiest combination to be due to both of the above groups of people.<br /> <br /> I want to say that many of the opinions on what is racist present here seem very lacking, and they avoid what is at the core of racism. Racism is an institution designed to maintain the power of the status quo, and combatting racism is going to be uncomfortable because combatting the status quo is uncomfortable. Now i know it is easy to return to the straw man argument against only white people being capable of racism, because it is a pretty ridiculous notion, but the fact that racism is an institution that permeates our media, our mores, and every aspect of our very lives means that every person has been indoctrinated into a culture of racism and everyone is racists, especially white people who are the main beneficiaries of the white supremacist status quo.<br /> <br /> I know that this is a disquieting notion, because racism is vile, and most people do not want to think of themselves as being intrinsically part of a vile system, but it really doesn't make sense to me when i see people who benefit from racism constantly denying their own participation in it, and by that i mean the system created by racism, when almost every poc i know is still dealing with the effects of internalized racism, even after years of working to get it out of their system.<br /> <br /> So no, white people are not the only ones who can be racist, i can personally attest to this after seeing plenty of poc who were racist towards different groups of poc, but that does not change the fact that white people are the ultimate beneficiaries of a system built on racism in the current world that we live in, and yea it may be terrible for people who have to face the consequences of their actions, but the response to this is not to be more accepting of racist behavior, but to provide systems through which people can work towards alleviating themselves of their racist culture.<br /> <br /> No one is born a racist, but in the world that we live in, it is almost a sure thing that people will be taught how to be that way very easily, and i do believe that the only way to reverse this indoctrination of white supremacy that everyone goes through to varying levels is through education (and by this i do not mean just any education as intellectuals are often just as racist as the uneducated if not more so, i mean a specific education in anti-racism), but people got to be willing to accept that they have a problem first, and that they will likely always have a problem that they have to constantly work on.<br /> <br /> Working to abolish the status quo if institutionalized white supremacy and racism is not a race where you can get to a finish line and stop working, it is a project that must be undertook by all people constantly so that some day in the future, we will have eradicated the traces of casual and overt racism from our collective culture so that future generations will not be indoctrinated into it in the same way that we have, and not have to make the same efforts that we do. My wife was raised in a world where the pinnacle of beauty was seen as a whiteness, and because of this she still doubts to this day whether or not she is as attractive as the most basic looking of white women when she is by far the more gorgeous woman i've ever seen, and inshallah i hope to raise daughters who are not raised with the same culture where european beauty standards and whiteness are seen as the paragon of humanity so that they will not have to deal with the same.<br /> <br /> anyways, i know this got a bit off topic and wasn't related to the original post about the movie, and i apologize for that, but i feel that it was related to the line of discussion that this thread followed, please forgive me if i have overstepped, i usually don't leave my specific forum.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> i saw your post after i submitted mine and i didn't want to double post so i'm just adding this to the end of this one but i feel like you said a bit of what i did a bit more succinctly than i did and i appreciate your addition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":1990,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","user":"norraba","date":". 04-27-2017, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T20:15:12-07:00","id":1084833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084659#post1084659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this seems like as good an opportunity as any to talk about something that's been on my mind. I don't know about elsewhere in the world, but here in the US, it seems we are in an awkward position thanks to racism being seen as a Special Kind of Evil. Granted, racially-based predjdice is not a good thing, but we kind of have a tendency to equate &amp;quot;racist&amp;quot; = &amp;quot;irredeemable monster&amp;quot;. Which makes it very difficult to call people out on minor things related to race. You can't say &amp;quot;hey, that joke you made kind of crossed a line for me&amp;quot; without the other person lashing out defensively because how dare you accuse them of being &amp;quot;a racist&amp;quot;. The concept of micro-aggressions isn't taken seriously because the idea that such minor things could make someone &amp;quot;a racist&amp;quot; seems inane. When really the point is that you don't have to be &amp;quot;a racist&amp;quot; to engage in racially insensitive behavior, and that doesn't make you a horrible person, but we would all do well to be mindful of those things and to make an effort to address them.<br /> <br /> I feel like Avenue Q had the right idea and took the wrong lesson from it.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's because microaggressions aren't a thing, some of us, and that includes none white people don't like having every little thing we say policed by an annoying college student who misinterrupt things in search of something to be agrrieved about.<br /> <br /> Its one of the many bad ideas coming from college campuses now, along with safe spaces, trigger warnings, free speech zones (which should be the whole campus not some corner you need to get an appointment too), checking privledge, and Kangeroo Courts where you guilty until proven innocent...oh wait that's right you not allowed to prove you innocence.<br /> <br /> This is like of stuff that Trump loves, its pisses normal people off and makes it easier for him to win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T20:24:37-07:00","id":1084835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084824#post1084824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something I've noticed as well. Its difficult to explain the concept of institutional racism and individual prejudice because we've created this image of a capital-R &quot;Racist&quot; with a Klan robe and a Nazi armband. A cartoon villain synonymous with evil. People think &quot;I can't be saying/doing something racist because that would make me a Racist and Racists Are Bad People. I'm not a bad person.&quot; We don't like shades of gray, we don't like self-reflection, and we like difficult solutions least of all. Its much easier to see the world as good people versus bad people, as opposed to a messy system of well-meaning people with prejudices they may not even be aware of that come out of cultural and historical baggage all making choices based on seemingly reasonable calculations and value judgments the aggregate of which still creates outcomes that are prejudicial and oppressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! Well said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084824#post1084824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've grown to hate the Avenue Q song. Not because of itself, but because of the meme its turned into. &quot;Everybody's a little bit racist... therefore whatever it is I'm doing that's perceived as racist doesn't really matter and whoever is complaining about it is a hypocrite.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully agree. But, like I said, I think it's drawing the wrong conclusions from the right realization. &quot;If we all could just admit that we are racist a little bit (...) maybe we could live in harmony!&quot; is actually a really valuable message. It's just the omitted part in the middle that's misguided. Accepting that we do have culturally ingrained racist tendencies allows us to better critically examine those tendencies, instead of trying to brush them under the rug as &quot;not<i> really</i> Racist&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T20:41:03-07:00","id":1084842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084833#post1084833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is like of stuff that Trump loves, its pisses normal people off and makes it easier for him to win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who are normal people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T20:42:51-07:00","id":1084844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084833#post1084833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's because microaggressions aren't a thing, some of us, and that includes none white people don't like having every little thing we say policed by an annoying college student who misinterrupt things in search of something to be agrrieved about.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;microaggressions aren't a thing&quot; isn't an argument, it's just a contradiction of the academically supported notion. I too can say &quot;yes they do&quot; and we won't get anywhere. My actual point, should you care to engage with it, is that subtle, indirect, and unintentional discrimination shouldn't need to be something college students police you about, it should be something you are aware happen and be self-reflective about. But, because people are too afraid of being labeled &quot;a racist&quot; to engage in critical self-reflection regarding culturally ingrained biases, they instead dismiss the idea that discrimination can be subtle, indirect, or unintentional <i>at all</i>, which is frankly ridiculous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084833#post1084833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its one of the many bad ideas coming from college campuses now, along with safe spaces, trigger warnings, free speech zones (which should be the whole campus not some corner you need to get an appointment too), checking privledge,</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I can say &quot;no, your ideas are bad!&quot; but that won't get us anywhere. At any rate, I think the mistrust of academia is a big problem in this country (yeah, I know, you're Canadian). These ideas are good ones, but often people who are not steeped in academia will rail against based on misunderstandings of their functions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084833#post1084833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and Kangeroo Courts where you guilty until proven innocent...oh wait that's right you not allowed to prove you innocence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what you're referring to here. Sounds made up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084833#post1084833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is like of stuff that Trump loves, its pisses normal people off and makes it easier for him to win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, yeah, we all know you think Donald's election is all the PC liberals' faults. This notion has been pretty thoroughly picked apart in other threads, I'm no longer interested in humoring it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-27-2017, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T22:44:10-07:00","id":1084898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084831#post1084831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its very interesting to me when I see people in gaming communities hold these types of conversations regarding race. Naturally, given the large number of white men who make up the table table top gaming genre, there are a lot of people like some on here (i won't name them specifically because i don't want to get banned and i have a feeling that mentioning people who are in their current situation might be a forum etiquette faux pa) who are so lost in their self supporting worldview that they have become convinced that white men are the real ones who are being persecuted by being expected to treat others as human beings for a change, and as many people have pointed out, they tend to sound like members of alt-right groups.<br /> <br /> then there are others who skirt the lines of apologist language, who don't agree with the alt-right sounding individuals, but want to make allowances for them, in politics they are often referred to as liberals, the moderates in the political spectrum who believe they are on the left simply because they are contrasted by the right.<br /> <br /> I am a person of color and a gamer, and i can tell you that this is not always the easiest combination to be due to both of the above groups of people.<br /> <br /> I want to say that many of the opinions on what is racist present here seem very lacking, and they avoid what is at the core of racism. Racism is an institution designed to maintain the power of the status quo, and combatting racism is going to be uncomfortable because combatting the status quo is uncomfortable. Now i know it is easy to return to the straw man argument against only white people being capable of racism, because it is a pretty ridiculous notion, but the fact that racism is an institution that permeates our media, our mores, and every aspect of our very lives means that every person has been indoctrinated into a culture of racism and everyone is racists, especially white people who are the main beneficiaries of the white supremacist status quo.<br /> <br /> I know that this is a disquieting notion, because racism is vile, and most people do not want to think of themselves as being intrinsically part of a vile system, but it really doesn't make sense to me when i see people who benefit from racism constantly denying their own participation in it, and by that i mean the system created by racism, when almost every poc i know is still dealing with the effects of internalized racism, even after years of working to get it out of their system.<br /> <br /> So no, white people are not the only ones who can be racist, i can personally attest to this after seeing plenty of poc who were racist towards different groups of poc, but that does not change the fact that white people are the ultimate beneficiaries of a system built on racism in the current world that we live in, and yea it may be terrible for people who have to face the consequences of their actions, but the response to this is not to be more accepting of racist behavior, but to provide systems through which people can work towards alleviating themselves of their racist culture.<br /> <br /> No one is born a racist, but in the world that we live in, it is almost a sure thing that people will be taught how to be that way very easily, and i do believe that the only way to reverse this indoctrination of white supremacy that everyone goes through to varying levels is through education (and by this i do not mean just any education as intellectuals are often just as racist as the uneducated if not more so, i mean a specific education in anti-racism), but people got to be willing to accept that they have a problem first, and that they will likely always have a problem that they have to constantly work on.<br /> <br /> Working to abolish the status quo if institutionalized white supremacy and racism is not a race where you can get to a finish line and stop working, it is a project that must be undertook by all people constantly so that some day in the future, we will have eradicated the traces of casual and overt racism from our collective culture so that future generations will not be indoctrinated into it in the same way that we have, and not have to make the same efforts that we do. My wife was raised in a world where the pinnacle of beauty was seen as a whiteness, and because of this she still doubts to this day whether or not she is as attractive as the most basic looking of white women when she is by far the more gorgeous woman i've ever seen, and inshallah i hope to raise daughters who are not raised with the same culture where european beauty standards and whiteness are seen as the paragon of humanity so that they will not have to deal with the same.<br /> <br /> anyways, i know this got a bit off topic and wasn't related to the original post about the movie, and i apologize for that, but i feel that it was related to the line of discussion that this thread followed, please forgive me if i have overstepped, i usually don't leave my specific forum.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> i saw your post after i submitted mine and i didn't want to double post so i'm just adding this to the end of this one but i feel like you said a bit of what i did a bit more succinctly than i did and i appreciate your addition.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you (and the others) call &quot;racist&quot; is simply people's natural positive bias toward their own &quot;tribe&quot; and negative bias toward the &quot;others&quot;. It's not a great evil white supremacy conspiracy designed to keep poc suppressed, it's just how the human brain is hardwired. That doesn't mean we shouldn't be aware of it and working against it (although it's hard sometimes, because not every culture is completely compatible with each other), but it's not intentional in most cases and it's not a &quot;system&quot;. Go to China as an European and you'll get the same experiences or worse. In that sense, yes everyone in the world is racist, but then we aren't speaking about the kind of racism which is indeed a crime and rightly so. It either makes a large group of people, nevertheless a whole culture guilty based on principle (and guess who did that in the past?), or it makes the term inconsequential.<br /> <br /> In that sense, the biggest crime of white people on the West is that they dare to be the majority and that it has implications, which yes, sadly frequently aren't positive toward the minorities. It should be better, but it won't with swiping generalizations and accusations of horrible things based on race, sex, etc.<br /> <br /> So, sorry, collective blaming just doesn't work in my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T23:19:20-07:00","id":1084902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084898#post1084898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you (and the others) call &amp;quot;racist&amp;quot; is simply people's natural positive bias toward their own &amp;quot;tribe&amp;quot; and negative bias toward the &amp;quot;others&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is. And because a few groups hold power over many other groups, that natural bias perpetuates the inequality between those groups even without malicious intent on the part of the groups in power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084898#post1084898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a great evil white supremacy conspiracy designed to keep poc suppressed, it's just how the human brain is hardwired.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is arguing that it is. Institutionalized injustice isn't willful malice, it's an unfortunate result of cognitive bias that we should be aware of and strive to counteract.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084898#post1084898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't mean we shouldn't be aware of it and working against it (although it's hard sometimes, because not every culture is completely compatible with each other), but it's not intentional in most cases</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084898#post1084898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and it's not a &amp;quot;system&amp;quot;. Go to China as an European and you'll get the same experiences or worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you may be misunderstanding what is meant by calling this inequality &quot;systematic&quot;. There is no consciously constructed system built with the purpose of prepetuating injustice. Rather, the social and political systems under which we operate were created with the afformentioned cognative bias by largely racially homogeneous groups, creating unconscios bias in favor of those groups within the systems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084898#post1084898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that sense, yes everyone in the world is racist, but then we aren't speaking about the kind of racism which is indeed a crime and rightly so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Accurate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084898#post1084898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It either makes a large group of people, nevertheless a whole culture guilty based on principle (and guess who did that in the past?), or it makes the term inconsequential.</div> </div> </div> </div>It forces us to acknowledge that people of certain groups reap the benefits of a biased system while others suffer under the bias inherent in the system, despite lack of malicious intent. It forces us to recognize that malicious intent is not a necessary feature of inequality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084898#post1084898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that sense, the biggest crime of white people on the West is that they dare to be the majority and that it has implications, which yes, sadly frequently aren't positive toward the minorities. It should be better, but it won't with swiping generalizations and accusations of horrible things based on race, sex, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point to begin with is that the issue here is the assumption that calling out subtle, indirect, unintentional discrimination equates to sweeping generalizations of horrible things. This is something that is being projected onto the message that racism is an institution, not the content of the message itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084898#post1084898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, sorry, collective blaming just doesn't work in my book.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that the systems, not the individuals, are to blame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T23:39:16-07:00","id":1084904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084902#post1084902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you may be misunderstanding what is meant by calling this inequality &quot;systematic&quot;. There is no consciously constructed system built with the purpose of prepetuating injustice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean. There have been, though. There still are. South Africa's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apartheid\" target=\"_blank\">apartheid</a>. The South's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Crow_laws\" target=\"_blank\">Jim Crow laws</a>. These were consciously constructed systems build with the purpose of discrimination. And it's happened again and again throughout history. The colonizations of the Americas and Africa, the caste system of India for an intra-racial version. The only thing keeping it from happening again and again is getting past 'natural' instincts, the same way we got past them in regards to leaving feeble babies to die of exposure, shitting in the corner, or going on murderous rampages in the name of vengeance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T00:03:56-07:00","id":1084910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084898#post1084898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you (and the others) call &quot;racist&quot; is simply people's natural positive bias toward their own &quot;tribe&quot; and negative bias toward the &quot;others&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that make it not racism?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not a great evil white supremacy conspiracy designed to keep poc suppressed, it's just how the human brain is hardwired. </div> </div> </div>In the USA? It's not that simple. Because our system is actually a white supremacist designed institution designed to keep PoC suppressed.<br /> <br /> The system was designed - completely on purpose - to make wealthy white land owners in low population agricultural states the most powerful people in the country so that diverse high population urban centers wouldn't dominate the political agenda of the nation. For all the progress we've made regarding civil rights, the institutions which were designed to keep white people in charge haven't actually changed on a fundamental level.<br /> <br /> Yes, there's some human brain hard wiring going on, but the failure to recognize that, and act against it because we are capable of doing so perpetuates a system that was designed to oppress PoC instead of allowing it to be fixed.<br /> <br /> It's what allows people to feel comfortable voting for politicians that overtly admit that they're making voting laws specifically to screw over minority voters. That needs to be changed. Every voter that doesn't allow themselves to draw a hard line on topics - like voter suppression - is allowing racism to continue. It might not be a conspiracy, but it's a status quo that takes work to change and they're not helping.<br /> <br /> The US system is inherently biased. Until that's fixed, regardless of any individuals intent, there is a system of racism here. No amount of Civil Rights laws, or media saturation of cultural messages, or whatever actually changes that. All those can do is empower the population to fix the system as it should be fixed to actually throw out the built in racism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Go to China as an European and you'll get the same experiences or worse. </div> </div> </div>Odd. What is this based on exactly?<br /> <br /> China (and a few other south east Asian countries) put a huge amount of systemic effort into making westerners feel welcome. They want tourists, business people, and so on to see an idealized China with a healthy but accepting culture, for the country's economic benefit.<br /> <br /> This was true decades ago before trade with China was normalized, and the Chinese government taught some very racist things about non-Chinese people*, but that was a long time ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In that sense, yes everyone in the world is racist, but then we aren't speaking about the kind of racism which is indeed a crime and rightly so. </div> </div> </div>Racism isn't a crime, because it's a belief. It's how people act that are crimes or not (or should be crimes when sometimes they aren't).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, sorry, collective blaming just doesn't work in my book. </div> </div> </div>What's the point of democracy if we can't acknowledge that we share collective blame for the actions of the collective state? Just because I don't vote for something doesn't mean I share no blame in what happens. It's a democracy. By valuing it, I value the power of the vote and the consequences therein.<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> * As an example, when I was a young kid we had a Chinese family visiting our family for Thanksgiving. They were shocked to see us treat my grandparents with respect and love, because they were raised to think that westerners don't respect their elders and dump the elderly in homes because we don't care about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T05:14:02-07:00","id":1084970,"title":"","content":"I hesitate to write anything, but what @'PM\u00e1rk' might talk about can be is better explained by Campbell in his realistic conflict theory. It also tries to explain the problems arising implementing diversity measures and imho opinion it shows what is going wrong with the US currently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T06:15:43-07:00","id":1084994,"title":"","content":"Realistic conflict theory doesn't take into account self-awareness or ideology. It only controls for what<i> external </i>factors motivate people to view ingroups and outgroups positively or negatively. Taken at face value, one might assume that integration is <i>impossible</i> unless superordinate goals are imposed on both groups, and history has shown us this is not so. Moral outrage has been the biggest driver of the civil rights movement since the Abolitionist days. <br /> <br /> In other words, &quot;it's a natural tendency for humans to behave like this&quot; is a weak excuse. Humans naturally tend to do a lot of things that society frowns on and tries to control for. I think it's perfectly reasonable to argue that our society <i>is not doing enough</i> to encourage cooperation between different ethnic groups, and that individual people <i>are </i>responsible for their action/inaction when it comes to combating racism. Conversely, laws and regulations <i>made specifically to prevent groups from integrating</i> <i>or gaining power </i>perpetuate divisions regardless of what other environmental factors might motivate people to come together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 04-28-2017, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T06:21:17-07:00","id":1084996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084904#post1084904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean. There have been, though. There still are. South Africa's <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apartheid&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">apartheid</a>. The South's <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Crow_laws&amp;quot;]Jim</a> Crow laws[/URL]. These were consciously constructed systems build with the purpose of discrimination. And it's happened again and again throughout history. The colonizations of the Americas and Africa, the caste system of India for an intra-racial version. The only thing keeping it from happening again and again is getting past 'natural' instincts, the same way we got past them in regards to leaving feeble babies to die of exposure, shitting in the corner, or going on murderous rampages in the name of vengeance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T14:08:46-07:00","id":1085137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084902#post1084902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it is. And because a few groups hold power over many other groups, that natural bias perpetuates the inequality between those groups even without malicious intent on the part of the groups in power.<br /> <br /> <br /> No one is arguing that it is. Institutionalized injustice isn't willful malice, it's an unfortunate result of cognitive bias that we should be aware of and strive to counteract.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yep.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think you may be misunderstanding what is meant by calling this inequality &quot;systematic&quot;. There is no consciously constructed system built with the purpose of prepetuating injustice. Rather, the social and political systems under which we operate were created with the afformentioned cognative bias by largely racially homogeneous groups, creating unconscios bias in favor of those groups within the systems.<br /> <br /> <br /> Accurate.<br /> <br /> <br /> It forces us to acknowledge that people of certain groups reap the benefits of a biased system while others suffer under the bias inherent in the system, despite lack of malicious intent. It forces us to recognize that malicious intent is not a necessary feature of inequality.<br /> <br /> <br /> My point to begin with is that the issue here is the assumption that calling out subtle, indirect, unintentional discrimination equates to sweeping generalizations of horrible things. This is something that is being projected onto the message that racism is an institution, not the content of the message itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> The point is that the systems, not the individuals, are to blame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'm glad we're mostly agree on that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd say, don't call it racism then. Racism is a serious accusation, with severe implications and this is not that. Call it favoritism, cultural bias, etc. and I will be okay with that.<br /> <br /> Criticizing the system(s) is okay, I'll support that and equality too. But saying &quot;all white people at racist&quot; is not a system criticism. Saying &quot; only white people could be racists&quot; is utterly ridiculous, because no, black/asian/green martian communities are doing the same. Saying things like that doesn't support discourse, it's actually the same methods racists use to shut down and marginalize minorities and I can't and won't support that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084910#post1084910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does that make it not racism?</div> </div> </div> </div>See my answer to Charlaquin. You could call it racism, but then indeed everyone is racist and people <i>will object, </i>because no, the majorit of them aren't Nazis. You could make arguments on the side of &quot;lesser kinds of racism&quot;, but good luck to get the society to acknowledge that instead of thinking about Nazis, slavers and certain African regimes!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the USA? It's not that simple. Because our system is actually a white supremacist designed institution designed to keep PoC suppressed.<br /> <br /> The system was designed - completely on purpose - to make wealthy white land owners in low population agricultural states the most powerful people in the country so that diverse high population urban centers wouldn't dominate the political agenda of the nation. For all the progress we've made regarding civil rights, the institutions which were designed to keep white people in charge haven't actually changed on a fundamental level.<br /> <br /> Yes, there's some human brain hard wiring going on, but the failure to recognize that, and act against it because we are capable of doing so perpetuates a system that was designed to oppress PoC instead of allowing it to be fixed.<br /> <br /> It's what allows people to feel comfortable voting for politicians that overtly admit that they're making voting laws specifically to screw over minority voters. That needs to be changed. Every voter that doesn't allow themselves to draw a hard line on topics - like voter suppression - is allowing racism to continue. It might not be a conspiracy, but it's a status quo that takes work to change and they're not helping.<br /> <br /> The US system is inherently biased. Until that's fixed, regardless of any individuals intent, there is a system of racism here. No amount of Civil Rights laws, or media saturation of cultural messages, or whatever actually changes that. All those can do is empower the population to fix the system as it should be fixed to actually throw out the built in racism. </div> </div> </div>That's actually an important thing! I could acknowledge that it's really a problem in the USA. I don't know, because I don't live there and not really know the voting system's nuances or the law in general, just what I see in the big media, so I'm willing to take it on just face value. BUT. The world is not consists only the USA and when someone says &quot;every white people are racist&quot; that implies me and other non-USA citizens too. We have our own problems, for example with the Roma minority and their integration. It has some parallels, but a lot of differences too with the state of poc minorities in the USA. We don't have a voting system designed to support slaver landowners either, because we never got those here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Odd. What is this based on exactly? </div> </div> </div>I can't give any paper on this. Mostly anecdotal evidence from friends working with Chinese and taking business trips there. Other Friend's ex living in Japan, their stories, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> China (and a few other south east Asian countries) put a huge amount of systemic effort into making westerners feel welcome. They want tourists, business people, and so on to see an idealized China with a healthy but accepting culture, for the country's economic benefit.<br /> <br /> This was true decades ago before trade with China was normalized, and the Chinese government taught some very racist things about non-Chinese people*, but that was a long time ago. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I bet this is the case as long as money is involved, but only as long as it's involved. I don't think they're better than us, honestly, I think on the contrary. It's another tendency nowadays, demonizing Western culture and idolizing other cultures, but honestly, we are still the most tolerant culture I think (I could be wrong).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Racism isn't a crime, because it's a belief. It's how people act that are crimes or not (or should be crimes when sometimes they aren't). </div> </div> </div>Although I'm not into law, I thought racist crimes are a thing and even an aggravating factor, no?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's the point of democracy if we can't acknowledge that we share collective blame for the actions of the collective state? Just because I don't vote for something doesn't mean I share no blame in what happens. It's a democracy. By valuing it, I value the power of the vote and the consequences therein. </div> </div> </div>You are free to believe in what you want. If you want to bash yourself for something you didn't do, feel free to do that! I won't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1084994#post1084994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Realistic conflict theory doesn't take into account self-awareness or ideology. It only controls for what<i> external </i>factors motivate people to view ingroups and outgroups positively or negatively. Taken at face value, one might assume that integration is <i>impossible</i> unless superordinate goals are imposed on both groups, and history has shown us this is not so. Moral outrage has been the biggest driver of the civil rights movement since the Abolitionist days.<br /> <br /> In other words, &quot;it's a natural tendency for humans to behave like this&quot; is a weak excuse. Humans naturally tend to do a lot of things that society frowns on and tries to control for. I think it's perfectly reasonable to argue that our society <i>is not doing enough</i> to encourage cooperation between different ethnic groups, and that individual people <i>are </i>responsible for their action/inaction when it comes to combating racism. Conversely, laws and regulations <i>made specifically to prevent groups from integrating</i> <i>or gaining power </i>perpetuate divisions regardless of what other environmental factors might motivate people to come together.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are good points. I agree that we should strive for working against certain instincts, including tribalism. However, I don't think tribalism on the same level as not taking what I want by bashing in my neighbor's skull and not pooing in the corner. Tribalism is more subtle and more pervasive and I'd argue it's not an entirely causeless evolutionary product.<br /> <br /> I also think it's ultimately impossible to eradicate. It's not only between races, but every kind of group of people in general. In places, which are melting pots, mostly cities and especially university cities, when you'll get a lot of people from a lot of different backgrounds and higher levels of education it'll ever be much loose (or you'll get just another kind of it), but in other parts, and especially in the country it'll be prevalent. Sorry, it's just like that.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying we shouldn't fight it, because I believe we should! We should educate, we should work hard on integrating minorities and treating everyone equally, but that won't be able with collective blaming and white hate. You'd just dig deeper trenches and that's what you're living in right now on the other side of the great pond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T15:31:12-07:00","id":1085179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1085137#post1085137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying we shouldn't fight it, because I believe we should! We should educate, we should work hard on integrating minorities and treating everyone equally, but that won't be able with collective blaming and white hate. You'd just dig deeper trenches and that's what you're living in right now on the other side of the great pond.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Come on, let's hug and make up!&quot;<br /> &quot;...You're holding a knife.&quot;<br /> &quot;Don't let that bother you.&quot;<br /> &quot;It has fresh blood and skin on it. Fuck's sake, what did you do, just skin someone? It doesn't look pale, either.&quot;<br /> &quot;Why are you so rude?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T16:06:26-07:00","id":1085208,"title":"","content":"&quot;Come on, why we can't be friends?&quot;<br /> &quot;You just robbed that shop. With a gun. And raped my niece last week.&quot;<br /> <br /> It goes either way.<br /> <br /> Besides, you realize that treating members of any given group on account of the worst, most extreme members of the group (especially with groups like race, which aren't chose-based), even when said members are shunned even by the community is... Kinda wrong?<br /> <br /> Look, I get historical grievances and such, but it leads nowhere but to more grievances on both sides and from extremism will born more extremism. Are you really want to live in perpetual hatred and war? Because that's what you'd get.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T17:16:34-07:00","id":1085238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1085208#post1085208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Come on, why we can't be friends?&quot;<br /> &quot;You just robbed that shop. With a gun. And raped my niece last week.&quot;<br /> <br /> It goes either way.<br /> <br /> Besides, you realize that treating members of any given group on account of the worst, most extreme members of the group (especially with groups like race, which aren't chose-based), even when said members are shunned even by the community is... Kinda wrong?<br /> <br /> Look, I get historical grievances and such, but it leads nowhere but to more grievances on both sides and from extremism will born more extremism. Are you really want to live in perpetual hatred and war? Because that's what you'd get.</div> </div> </div> </div>That simultaneously doesn't sound like anything resembling the historical or modern context of race relations in America(along side issues of class, economics and education that is directly tied to the issue of race in America) and unrealistic hyperbole. Also, as a white person, I find the idea of some massive, influential, meaningful wave of &quot;white hate.&quot; sweeping through America laughable and insulting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T18:39:09-07:00","id":1085265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1085179#post1085179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Come on, let's hug and make up!&quot;<br /> &quot;...You're holding a knife.&quot;<br /> &quot;Don't let that bother you.&quot;<br /> &quot;It has fresh blood and skin on it. Fuck's sake, what did you do, just skin someone? It doesn't look pale, either.&quot;<br /> &quot;Why are you so rude?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>When you have so many bloody weapons lying around from skinning people your black friends don't want to come over. #whitepeopleproblems","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T20:58:30-07:00","id":1085334,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of, 'I don't agree with these people, so they should shut up.' With some 'they should die or be arrested' interspersed in these threads, not just this one.<br /> <br /> And I get it.<br /> <br /> I don't like people complaining. Pointing out problems I don't necessarily have to deal with, and couldn't do anything about anyways.<br /> <br /> But at the other end of things, if people don't stand up, these things go on and on and on. 'Why didn't you say something sooner?' 'That's a once in a blue moon thing.' And we've seen crimes that have gone unreported for years and years because people didn't want to make a fuss. Institutions of callous indifference that go on and on because people don't want to kick over a rotting log and see the bugs underneath. The state I'm currently living in had a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eugenics_Board_of_North_Carolina\" target=\"_blank\">Eugenics Board</a> that forcibly sterilized people well into the 70s. And while it was outwardly for the 'public good,' to keep people from becoming burdens of the state, the truth is it started targeting non-whites in disproportionate numbers, considering their population.<br /> <br /> And yes, not every white person was going out and doing these things. And plenty of doctors didn't want to do it or get involved, but it still happened.<br /> <br /> Even more recently, the same state, after laws and time had passed that allowed more and more people to vote until POC were voting near to the level that whites were, the state legislature flat out requested data on how people voted, <i>by race</i>, then 'enacted legislation that restricted voting and registration in five different ways, all of which disproportionately affected African Americans.'<br /> <br /> These are things people do in our modern times. Sure, some of it is simply borne from an, 'us versus them' mentality, but we're not animals, and biases have been shown to be things people can get over. But it's not something that's ever going to go away if it's never acknowledged in the first place.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the show is on Netflix now. I've only watched one episode but so far its better than a lot of their other originals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T14:58:35-07:00","id":1085598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1085137#post1085137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are free to believe in what you want. If you want to bash yourself for something you didn't do, feel free to do that! I won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot believe this even needed to be said. But...here we are.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On topic, I checked out the first episode. Interesting, but not my kind of show. Though I knew that going in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T09:07:09-07:00","id":1085805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1085179#post1085179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Come on, let's hug and make up!&quot;<br /> &quot;...You're holding a knife.&quot;<br /> &quot;Don't let that bother you.&quot;<br /> &quot;It has fresh blood and skin on it. Fuck's sake, what did you do, just skin someone? It doesn't look pale, either.&quot;<br /> &quot;Why are you so rude?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1085208#post1085208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Come on, why we can't be friends?&quot;<br /> &quot;You just robbed that shop. With a gun. And raped my niece last week.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, Jesus Christ. Even if you're not from the States, that statement drips racist sterotypes so purely that even I, who lives in the deep south, am <i>impressed</i>.<br /> <br /> It was actually bad enough that I'm responding to this thread even though it's probably going to end up being a tire fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It goes either way.<br /> <br /> Besides, you realize that treating members of any given group on account of the worst, most extreme members of the group (especially with groups like race, which aren't chose-based), even when said members are shunned even by the community is... Kinda wrong?<br /> <br /> Look, I get historical grievances and such, but it leads nowhere but to more grievances on both sides and from extremism will born more extremism. Are you really want to live in perpetual hatred and war? Because that's what you'd get. </div> </div> </div>I'm familiar, yes, with how race-apathetic white people will cheerfully fall in lockstep with actively racist white people. I mean, Dr Martin Luther King talked about it once:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have almost reached the regrettable conclusion that the Negro's great stumbling block in his stride toward freedom is not the White Citizen's Counciler or the Ku Klux Klanner, but the white moderate, who is more devoted to &quot;order&quot; than to justice; who prefers a negative peace which is the absence of tension to a positive peace which is the presence of justice; who constantly says: &quot;I agree with you in the goal you seek, but I cannot agree with your methods of direct action&quot;; who paternalistically believes he can set the timetable for another man's freedom; who lives by a mythical concept of time and who constantly advises the Negro to wait for a &quot;more convenient season.&quot; Shallow understanding from people of good will is more frustrating than absolute misunderstanding from people of ill will. Lukewarm acceptance is much more bewildering than outright rejection. </div> </div> </div>The idea that we should just bury the hatchet is.. misguided. You're not from the States, as I understand, so you may not be familiar with how that's failed to work- Every time something happened in history that upset the white power structure, the underlying cause of it was never addressed; so it just continued.<br /> <br /> Slavery was ended (at least some of it, hold on); then white people in the south immediately set out to put black Americans back in the place white society had allotted for them. Laws crushed them into the dust and denied them the freedom and power to change or impact the class structure.<br /> <br /> After trials and tribulations, they get the right to vote, but then the racism just gets more rarefied. Gerrymandering that claims to not be racist, gutting of the voting rights act, the careful manipulation of school funds, job discrimination, police violence, feeding people into a prison-industry as cheap labor...<br /> <br /> Racism never dies because we never address it. We ignore it and push it away and pretend it's finally gone; because of that fail to notice how it impacts the country. It just gets more subtle, more rarefied.<br /> <br /> Slavery may be over, the civil rights era may be over, but the shadows those things cast continue to haunt the US. History never dies because it feeds the future. We are the product of the culture we live in, we are the children of the generations that came before us.<br /> <br /> We are the emergent property of the actions and events of the past.<br /> <br /> That's why ignoring them; and, refusing to admit there's a problem won't just make it go away.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T10:19:19-07:00","id":1085817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1085805#post1085805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, Jesus Christ. Even if you're not from the States, that statement drips racist sterotypes so purely that even I, who lives in the deep south, am <i>impressed</i>.<br /> <br /> It was actually bad enough that I'm responding to this thread even though it's probably going to end up being a tire fire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm familiar, yes, with how race-apathetic white people will cheerfully fall in lockstep with actively racist white people. I mean, Dr Martin Luther King talked about it once:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The idea that we should just bury the hatchet is.. misguided. You're not from the States, as I understand, so you may not be familiar with how that's failed to work- Every time something happened in history that upset the white power structure, the underlying cause of it was never addressed; so it just continued.<br /> <br /> Slavery was ended (at least some of it, hold on); then white people in the south immediately set out to put black Americans back in the place white society had allotted for them. Laws crushed them into the dust and denied them the freedom and power to change or impact the class structure.<br /> <br /> After trials and tribulations, they get the right to vote, but then the racism just gets more rarefied. Gerrymandering that claims to not be racist, gutting of the voting rights act, the careful manipulation of school funds, job discrimination, police violence, feeding people into a prison-industry as cheap labor...<br /> <br /> Racism never dies because we never address it. We ignore it and push it away and pretend it's finally gone; because of that fail to notice how it impacts the country. It just gets more subtle, more rarefied.<br /> <br /> Slavery may be over, the civil rights era may be over, but the shadows those things cast continue to haunt the US. History never dies because it feeds the future. We are the product of the culture we live in, we are the children of the generations that came before us.<br /> <br /> We are the emergent property of the actions and events of the past.<br /> <br /> That's why ignoring them; and, refusing to admit there's a problem won't just make it go away.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is why we <i>have to</i> call culturally-ingrained systemic bias racism. If we don't acknowledge the problem for what it is, it will never get fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T10:44:22-07:00","id":1085822,"title":"","content":"I saw the rest of the show. I'd have to agree that the jump to call it racist against white people was misguided.<br /> <br /> While the show itself doesn't really bring to light any new issues, it shows the issues people, not just black people, have with trying to deal with racism, and depicts it in an interesting and often amusing light. Especially the 'being drowned out by other voices,' which is a problem that's cropped up a lot lately. Through Gabe, each episode focusing on the point of view of one of the characters and him being the white one, we see his own problems in being 'a white face in a mostly black part of an overwhelmingly white place,' and dealing with jokes about his race while 'dodging the landmines of identity politics.' Good acting, all around, except with the oral sex. Very interesting and deep characters, when showcased, and I'm hoping we see more in season 2, particularly of Rashid, Joelle and Al. It's easy to dismiss characters as shallow but once you see them from different views it's clear there's a lot more to them, which was likely the point.<br /> <br /> Probably the most real aspect of the show, beyond the college-age angst, is that there's a dozen different people with different, often diametrically opposed, ways of dealing with their situation and no one has an easy answer that would work for everyone.<br /> <br /> Likely the best 'dramedy' I've ever seen, though it's not a genre I've seen much of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-30-2017, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T17:45:40-07:00","id":1085969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1085805#post1085805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> First of all, Jesus Christ. Even if you're not from the States, that statement drips racist sterotypes so purely that even I, who lives in the deep south, am <i>impressed</i>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I'm perfectly aware of that and it was intentional, since the part I'm responded to was also reeked stereotypes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm familiar, yes, with how race-apathetic white people will cheerfully fall in lockstep with actively racist white people. I mean, Dr Martin Luther King talked about it once:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The idea that we should just bury the hatchet is.. misguided. You're not from the States, as I understand, so you may not be familiar with how that's failed to work- Every time something happened in history that upset the white power structure, the underlying cause of it was never addressed; so it just continued.<br /> <br /> Slavery was ended (at least some of it, hold on); then white people in the south immediately set out to put black Americans back in the place white society had allotted for them. Laws crushed them into the dust and denied them the freedom and power to change or impact the class structure.<br /> <br /> After trials and tribulations, they get the right to vote, but then the racism just gets more rarefied. Gerrymandering that claims to not be racist, gutting of the voting rights act, the careful manipulation of school funds, job discrimination, police violence, feeding people into a prison-industry as cheap labor...<br /> <br /> Racism never dies because we never address it. We ignore it and push it away and pretend it's finally gone; because of that fail to notice how it impacts the country. It just gets more subtle, more rarefied.<br /> <br /> Slavery may be over, the civil rights era may be over, but the shadows those things cast continue to haunt the US. History never dies because it feeds the future. We are the product of the culture we live in, we are the children of the generations that came before us.<br /> <br /> We are the emergent property of the actions and events of the past.<br /> <br /> That's why ignoring them; and, refusing to admit there's a problem won't just make it go away. </div> </div> </div>Look, I'm not saying you shouldn't fight for equality. You should. But you should fight <i>for equality,</i> not <i>against other (in his case white) people</i>. Because you kick back, then they would kick back and on and on and you just strengthened the tribalism instead of alleviating it. <br /> <br /> Believe me, I'm on the side of equal rights, of equal opportunities, of equal treating by law-enforcement, for the sake of the flying Spaghetti Monster! I was honestly angered about the unprovoked shootings of black people by the police.<br /> <br /> I'm also not saying you don't have a problem there. While I see a lot of black people on different mediums, on videos from campuses, etc. I don't really see much black politicians from the US in the news, besides the last president, and it's concerning, just as the statistics of drug use, crime rates, poverty, lack of education, etc. among black communities (although some of what I remember might be out of date). You clearly have a problem, but collective blaming and trying to induce a culture of self-hate (I exaggerate, but it's late, please forgive me) among the white population won't solve that, it just creates more push-back and more antagonism. Again, I'm not saying 'don't do anything', I'm just saying, I'm pretty sure the current tendencies won't end well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T18:21:04-07:00","id":1085984,"title":"","content":"There is a world of difference between recognizing that we all have unconscious biases that perpetuate inequality and &quot;creating a culture of self-hate&quot;. One can recognize that one has culturally-ingrained racist tendencies and not hate themselves for it. In fact, doing so is an important step towards addressing and hopefully overcoming those subtle biases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T19:01:32-07:00","id":1085996,"title":"","content":"This came up in the show, as well. There's an argument when someone starts singing along with a song and a character asks them not to say a certain word because it's offensive. The singer gets defensive and wants to make it clear that he's not a racist, and the other character points out that they didn't think he is, that they're friends, and he didn't say that he was a racist to begin with. As the tension escalates and slavery gets mentioned, Rashid says, 'This is what happens when a country refuses to address its history with slavery,' and another character adds, 'We need to do here what they did in Germany.' Which gathers a collective, 'What!?' And he notes, 'I meant the education kids about the nation's horrible past part, not the concentration camp part.'<br /> <br /> Yes, history can be used as a weapon to flog people with. But just teaching it, educating people about the rights and wrongs of it, is a fair way to keep these things from happening again as well as help people understand why communities might feel marginalized or otherwise affected by it.<br /> <br /> We record history in part so we can avoid making the mistakes of the past. Ignoring certain parts of it because they're particularly ugly is missing the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T19:56:50-07:00","id":1086015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1085996#post1085996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This came up in the show, as well. There's an argument when someone starts singing along with a song and a character asks them not to say a certain word because it's offensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny. My brother was in that situation. A couple of years ago, his friend's family was hosting an exchange student, a Muslim from Albania named Blerim. Blerim loved rap music and had a really hard time understanding when my brother tried to explain to him that singing the n-word in public was <i>not</i> a good idea. &quot;But I have nothing to do with what some assholes in your country did to black people. I'm from a different country and follow a different religion and none of my family has been to the US before. But I'm not allowed to sing this song because my skin is white? Isn't that racist?&quot;<br /> <br /> And it was like, yeah, that's about it. My brother and I had to explain to him that, because he was white, and in America, and because of white American's actions, some people would get the wrong idea when he, a white dude, was using words like that, even in a song. They'd just see a white guy using the n-word and probably would never realize that he was from another country and had nothing to do with past events.<br /> <br /> He picked up on white privilege pretty quickly though. He noticed how fast people's attitudes would shift the moment they found out he was Muslim, and it wasn't hard for him to imagine how people would have treated him if he'd had darker skin and an Arabic name.<br /> <br /> But even after he left he told me he still found many of the ideas of race in America, and what's acceptable and what isn't acceptable, and who can say something and who can't say something to be incredibly confusing and often arbitrary. We had some interesting conversations though, and it really made me sit down and spend some time thinking about race in a way that I probably never would have done otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T20:18:03-07:00","id":1086024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086015#post1086015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'd just see a white guy using the n-word and probably would never realize that he was from another country and had nothing to do with past events.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I get what you mean, it's hardly anchored in its roots. Its use as a racial slur came later, and is still used to insult and belittle people in modern times, despite decades of attempting to reappropriate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T20:30:46-07:00","id":1086036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086024#post1086024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I get what you mean, it's hardly anchored in its roots. Its use as a racial slur came later, and is still used to insult and belittle people in modern times, despite decades of attempting to reappropriate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>By past events I meant things that had happened before he had arrived in the country (which, at the time, he'd only been here for a week or two).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T13:16:24-07:00","id":1086306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086015#post1086015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But even after he left he told me he still found many of the ideas of race in America, and what's acceptable and what isn't acceptable, and who can say something and who can't say something to be incredibly confusing and often arbitrary. We had some interesting conversations though, and it really made me sit down and spend some time thinking about race in a way that I probably never would have done otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an outsider, I could agree with him. You just have a strange land and a strange society, with a tendency toward self-absorbedness (in general, not you, specific people). A lot of the times, me and every one of my friends are standing still, shaking our heads, muttering 'Americans' with a sigh. It's not that the US is bad (I'm particularly grateful for rpgs, for example and a lot of other things I love), it's just... from our standpoint you people are just inclined to take everything to the extreme.<br /> <br /> For example, some of my friends are just bewildered about the whole social justice war, because they just don't read/watch American news sources, forums with mainly American people on it, etc. and they just don't encountered with it to that extent and one of them is even a homosexual. Yes, we have the somewhat same problems here, but the whole discussion is a lot more moderate, from all sides, most of the time. To be honest, what's going on at campuses in the past few yeas is just seeming to be way overboard and downright hysterical sometimes. I might add the above is equally true for both the right and the left.<br /> <br /> Oh, and about Germany, that's actually a good example for wallowing in self-hate. Like, today they don't dare to be proud of anything 'German'. Honestly, try to imagine the exact opposite of the usual American patriotism. It's not healthy and they did several very bad decisions about the migration crisis partly due to that, in the past years and I say it as someone who was firmly on the side of &quot;we should help them&quot; and very firmly against Orb\u00e1n's standpoint, but Germany did it without thinking it through. At least they revised it since then. It's a good thing they faced their past and all that, but they went with it to the other extreme and it1s bad too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-01-2017, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T13:37:51-07:00","id":1086310,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that the media here is essentially rewarded for making things look extreme, because extreme sells and accurate moderate coverage doesn't. Which is our society's fault and all, but you're seeing a snap shot of a snap shot in many cases, and which leaves things looking very different from how they actually are.<br /> <br /> Like, the whole college campus thing... it's nothing new, and nothing extreme. &quot;Safe spaces&quot; have pretty much always been a thing on college campuses, they just used to go by other names. Protesting speakers has gone on for decades. Etc. If you actually spend time with these people, you quickly find out the media representation of them is about as accurate as your average police action movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T13:52:20-07:00","id":1086319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086310#post1086310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that the media here is essentially rewarded for making things look extreme, because extreme sells and accurate moderate coverage doesn't. Which is our society's fault and all, but you're seeing a snap shot of a snap shot in many cases, and which leaves things looking very different from how they actually are.<br /> <br /> Like, the whole college campus thing... it's nothing new, and nothing extreme. &quot;Safe spaces&quot; have pretty much always been a thing on college campuses, they just used to go by other names. Protesting speakers has gone on for decades. Etc. If you actually spend time with these people, you quickly find out the media representation of them is about as accurate as your average police action movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Media is always doing that, everywhere. It's not only that, but blogs, FB, Tumblr, forums, YT channels, etc. etc. And there are speaks on marches, protests and such without commentary.<br /> <br /> It's highly probable that we're seeing only a fraction of the whole, and likely the most extreme parts, because yes, that's what people are talking about, but we're seeing a concerningly big amount of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T14:42:36-07:00","id":1086339,"title":"","content":"While people can debate its success, that's the whole point of Dear White People being made. To try to create media representations that more honestly (within the realm of fiction obviously) represent what things are really like. You see the same thing in movies like Get Out. These are creative people trying to paint a picture that counters the news media's push towards extreme representation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T14:56:44-07:00","id":1086345,"title":"","content":"But that's what I'm saying, it's not just the news media, but what and how people are saying around the internet. Not specifically here, honestly, this forum is among the most civilized places I frequent, despite all the heated arguments, but most people around there at least want to keep a civil discussion and argue and explain.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, what &quot;people are saying around he internet&quot; might be just a very vocal, but minor extreme part of the whole, but still.<br /> <br /> Another example: I have a friend, who defines herself as a feminist and an LBGTQ person. I had some arguments with her about my not so-flattering opinion on the social justice and feminist movement's present. Then she added me to the FB group she's in and they were all in all very nice and quite sensible and it turned out they tend to criticize the same stuff that made me cringe. So that highlighted that I don't have problems with them, I have problems with the extremes the internet is full of today.<br /> <br /> So again, I don't see how it is in the everyday life in the USA, my perception might be quite askew, but what I see from here, it's not very good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-01-2017, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T18:47:28-07:00","id":1086414,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to comment on the argument being had here, but if anyone wants to read more about the rise of mass incarceration and recent systematic racism, Elizabeth Hinton from Harvard wrote a really good book called <i>From the War on Poverty to the War on Crime</i>. It's about how despite how we typically think of Nixon and Reagan as starting the ridiculous mass incarceration rates we see now, where 1 in 11 black men are in prison, it actually started with Kennedy and LBJ encoding racist policies into juvenile delinquency and Great Society programs based on the assumption that black communities could not take care of themselves and required police involvement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 05-01-2017, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T18:53:53-07:00","id":1086416,"title":"","content":"Here's a clip of Hinton discussing her research.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=axA359s1cFE\" data-code=\"axA359s1cFE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/axA359s1cFE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T19:00:03-07:00","id":1086417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086345#post1086345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So again, I don't see how it is in the everyday life in the USA, my perception might be quite askew, but what I see from here, it's not very good.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the everyday, it's usually fine. Usually. <br /> <br /> Then, every so often, something happens. A legislature puts out a rule that seems to discriminate against minority voters. Cops shoot a black person in an avoidable confrontation. Somebody tags a Islamic or Jewish community building with slurs or swastikas. And that sets off a wave of paranoia and outrage which echoes in all directions. <br /> <br /> People who perceive themselves as underprivileged (whether they're right or wrong) lash out. The privileged folk who don't take their side get angry and defensive. Everyone tries to find someone or something to blame. Very, very rarely will anyone own up to making some kind of mistake and develop a plan to become better. <br /> <br /> That said, it has been worse in the past than it is today. The internet has a way of amplifying everyone's grievances and pushing people to extremes, but at least for now we're not dealing with the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1992_Los_Angeles_riots\" target=\"_blank\">Rodney King riots</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T19:03:47-07:00","id":1086419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086417#post1086417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the everyday, it's usually fine. Usually.<br /> <br /> Then, every so often, something happens. A legislature puts out a rule that seems to discriminate against minority voters. Cops shoot a black person in an avoidable confrontation. Somebody tags a Islamic or Jewish community building with slurs or swastikas. And that sets off a wave of paranoia and outrage which echoes in all directions.<br /> <br /> People who perceive themselves as underprivileged (whether they're right or wrong) lash out. The privileged folk who don't take their side get angry and defensive. Everyone tries to find someone or something to blame. Very, very rarely will anyone own up to making some kind of mistake and develop a plan to become better.<br /> <br /> That said, it has been worse in the past than it is today. The internet has a way of amplifying everyone's grievances and pushing people to extremes, but at least for now we're not dealing with the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1992_Los_Angeles_riots\" target=\"_blank\">Rodney King riots</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if the LEAA hadn't funded riot gear and literal tanks, those uprisings might not have escalated as they did anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T19:04:41-07:00","id":1086420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086015#post1086015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funny. My brother was in that situation. A couple of years ago, his friend's family was hosting an exchange student, a Muslim from Albania named Blerim. Blerim loved rap music and had a really hard time understanding when my brother tried to explain to him that singing the n-word in public was <i>not</i> a good idea. &quot;But I have nothing to do with what some assholes in your country did to black people. I'm from a different country and follow a different religion and none of my family has been to the US before. But I'm not allowed to sing this song because my skin is white? Isn't that racist?&quot;<br /> <br /> And it was like, yeah, that's about it. My brother and I had to explain to him that, because he was white, and in America, and because of white American's actions, some people would get the wrong idea when he, a white dude, was using words like that, even in a song. They'd just see a white guy using the n-word and probably would never realize that he was from another country and had nothing to do with past events.<br /> <br /> He picked up on white privilege pretty quickly though. He noticed how fast people's attitudes would shift the moment they found out he was Muslim, and it wasn't hard for him to imagine how people would have treated him if he'd had darker skin and an Arabic name.<br /> <br /> But even after he left he told me he still found many of the ideas of race in America, and what's acceptable and what isn't acceptable, and who can say something and who can't say something to be incredibly confusing and often arbitrary. We had some interesting conversations though, and it really made me sit down and spend some time thinking about race in a way that I probably never would have done otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are a lot of things to reply to in this, so i'll start from the top:<br /> America is not the only country in the world with a history of antiblackness, in fact most countries in the world have a history of antiblackness. White people are not the only people with a history of antiblackness either, and most peoples on the planet have their own version of the n-word.<br /> Going from there, even though eastern europeans, and espeacially the muslim eastern europeans, are persecuted and discrimintated against through xenophobia by western europeans, they still have a strong history of antiblackness, and the middle east does as well, with the most commonly used arabic word for a black person meaning slave due to the arab and muslim slave trade that was contemproraies with the american and european slave trade.<br /> <br /> So it is not just that the n-word is not something that white people can say, it is something that no one who isn't black should say, that includes non-black poc, and the idea that his guy didnt know the meaning or the implication behind the word is a bit ludicrous, unless he was an exceptionally ignorant person. <br /> <br /> like witht he case of using slurs like the n-word, its not like people are specifically trying to attack white peopel by not letting them use it, no one outside of the group that the slur is used as a pejorative towards should ever use the slur, because slurs are inherantly biggoted in their meanign and thier usage, save for when they are reclaimed by the people who were originally facing the violence of the pejorative statement. like its not like this is an america only thing, and i know that this mentality exists in canada as well so pretending that it doesnt make sense to peopel from other countries is ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T19:05:28-07:00","id":1086421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086417#post1086417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the everyday, it's usually fine. Usually.<br /> <br /> Then, every so often, something happens. A legislature puts out a rule that seems to discriminate against minority voters. Cops shoot a black person in an avoidable confrontation. Somebody tags a Islamic or Jewish community building with slurs or swastikas. And that sets off a wave of paranoia and outrage which echoes in all directions.<br /> <br /> People who perceive themselves as underprivileged (whether they're right or wrong) lash out. The privileged folk who don't take their side get angry and defensive. Everyone tries to find someone or something to blame. Very, very rarely will anyone own up to making some kind of mistake and develop a plan to become better.<br /> <br /> That said, it has been worse in the past than it is today. The internet has a way of amplifying everyone's grievances and pushing people to extremes, but at least for now we're not dealing with the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1992_Los_Angeles_riots\" target=\"_blank\">Rodney King riots</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the summary, it sounds sensible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T19:12:26-07:00","id":1086427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086420#post1086420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are a lot of things to reply to in this, so i'll start from the top:<br /> America is not the only country in the world with a history of antiblackness, in fact most countries in the world have a history of antiblackness. White people are not the only people with a history of antiblackness either, and most peoples on the planet have their own version of the n-word.<br /> Going from there, even though eastern europeans, and espeacially the muslim eastern europeans, are persecuted and discrimintated against through xenophobia by western europeans, they still have a strong history of antiblackness, and the middle east does as well, with the most commonly used arabic word for a black person meaning slave due to the arab and muslim slave trade that was contemproraies with the american and european slave trade.<br /> <br /> So it is not just that the n-word is not something that white people can say, it is something that no one who isn't black should say, that includes non-black poc, and the idea that his guy didnt know the meaning or the implication behind the word is a bit ludicrous, unless he was an exceptionally ignorant person.<br /> <br /> like witht he case of using slurs like the n-word, its not like people are specifically trying to attack white peopel by not letting them use it, no one outside of the group that the slur is used as a pejorative towards should ever use the slur, because slurs are inherantly biggoted in their meanign and thier usage, save for when they are reclaimed by the people who were originally facing the violence of the pejorative statement. like its not like this is an america only thing, and i know that this mentality exists in canada as well so pretending that it doesnt make sense to peopel from other countries is ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with this is not that it isn't true, but how often those kind of reasoning focuses only on what white people do, while in reality, everyone does that, every ethnicity has biases toward their own and against others. <br /> <br /> Often, it's resulting in demonizing white people, while idolizing other races and cultures. No, the &quot;others did the same&quot; isn't a redeemer for anything, I said that in an older thread and I still think that, but accentuating only one side of the things is also discrimination.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T19:13:59-07:00","id":1086429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1085984#post1085984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a world of difference between recognizing that we all have unconscious biases that perpetuate inequality and &quot;creating a culture of self-hate&quot;. One can recognize that one has culturally-ingrained racist tendencies and not hate themselves for it. In fact, doing so is an important step towards addressing and hopefully overcoming those subtle biases.</div> </div> </div> </div>i've noticed that for many people, the idea of recognizing these tendendcies at all seems like a matter of self hate, primarily becasue the goal of reformative and revolutionary action alike should be the removal of privliage, not the giving of privliage to all peoples.<br /> <br /> To explain what i mean by this we can take the example of the the chinese american cop peter liang who shot an unarmed black person. the response of the chinese comunity to this was not outrage at the extrajucial execution of someone who was black, but anger that he was being charged for it, when white cops get away with doing the very same thing all the time. This is not progress, it is the struggle of certain groups of the opressed to attain opressor status, and the opposite of what progressive race relations looks like.<br /> <br /> what progressive race relations looks like would be the holding to acount all white cops who execute people extrajudicialy, and the elimination of all privliages enjoyed by white people, so that things will truely be on an even playing field, but for many people, the taking away of their privliages seems like an egregious crime against them, and so to want to do anything of the sort they reason, a person must be self hating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T19:22:51-07:00","id":1086431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086427#post1086427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem with this is not that it isn't true, but how often those kind of reasoning focuses only on what white people do, while in reality, everyone does that, every ethnicity has biases toward their own and against others.<br /> <br /> Often, it's resulting in demonizing white people, while idolizing other races and cultures. No, the &quot;others did the same&quot; isn't a redeemer for anything, I said that in an older thread and I still think that, but accentuating only one side of the things is also discrimination.</div> </div> </div> </div>much of this discussion focusses on white people because we are having this discussion in the west, and it is to the majority white people who do these things in the west, but regardless of this, im am calling out non-white groups and marginally white groups in the post you quoted and the post i made right after yours also has a case of me calling out non-white groups.<br /> <br /> That said, due to the histroy of global colonialism by white poeple, there is an aspect of white supremacy world wide, and not just in the areas where white poeple are the majority, with the perfect example being how european beuaty standards being seen as the most desireable as if white people are just inherantly better looking than everyone else.<br /> <br /> we accentuate white racism becasue it is the most predominant, even on an overall international level, and just because we need to be willing to call out racism against other poc by different groups of poc does not mean we pretend intra-poc racism is just being ignored by everyone in order to vilify white poeple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T19:52:20-07:00","id":1086440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086427#post1086427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Often, it's resulting in demonizing white people, while idolizing other races and cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a common concern but not really the point of the socially progressive agenda, and I'd argue that it's falling into the trap covered before in the thread, with the 'no middle ground' when it comes to racism.<br /> <br /> You, and Tobias, have brought up the idea that people are saying, 'all white people are racist.' But that's not what's being said. Just like in the show, 'No one said you were racist.' We're just all part of this system, and it's a system of inequality, where some people are already idolized and others are already demonized. Working to cut out the demonization and idolization is how we're attempting to get to equality, where people would be treated according to their character, and not the color of their skin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T21:40:23-07:00","id":1086462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086440#post1086440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a common concern but not really the point of the socially progressive agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. The majority of the criticisms against social progressivism strike me as criticisms of straw-arguments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T21:50:42-07:00","id":1086466,"title":"","content":"As a white person, as a dual citizen, as a military veteran, as a father of a soon to be teenager, as a bisexual man, as someone whose had a firearm pointed at him, as someone whose been stabbed before, as someone whose starved and been poor most of his life. I care just a wee bit more the intersectionality of ethnicity, economic freedom, environmental safety, and civil rights against the vast threat to those things by vested, powerful institutions and individuals around the globe who actually do have great power and are using it to destroy those things, than I do people complaining that some students at university somewhere have wonky notions of free speech, or that some white people are uncomfortable confronting the part they play, as a member of society, in the perpetuation of institutional prejudices. So well put by the reference to MLK's thoughts on those individuals. Their righteous indignation is not worth the cost in the misery that is paid daily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T22:51:36-07:00","id":1086483,"title":"","content":"I don't got the emotional energy to argue in this kind of thread. Thank you for putting that in words though.<br /> <br /> Their righteous indignation is not worth the cost in the misery that is paid daily.<br /> <br /> It's kind of crazy that we live in a society where the act of calling out racism or the accusation that it might be occurring is frequently compared with <i>racism itself</i>. <br /> <br /> I feel like that is a far more salient point to consider in asking questions about hypersensitivity in contemporary living.<br /> <br /> I would not wish the experiences I've had on anyone. Yet, sometimes I wish I could, if only for a moment, so that people could intuitively understand how ridiculous it is to compare the accusation of racism with racism itself.<br /> <br /> It's a lot like people reacting so strongly to a show because it's entitled <i>Dear White People</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T23:12:44-07:00","id":1086487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086483#post1086483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't got the emotional energy to argue in this kind of thread. Thank you for putting that in words though.<br /> <br /> Their righteous indignation is not worth the cost in the misery that is paid daily.<br /> <br /> It's kind of crazy that we live in a society where the act of calling out racism or the accusation that it might be occurring is frequently compared with <i>racism itself</i>.<br /> <br /> I feel like that is a far more salient point to consider in asking questions about hypersensitivity in contemporary living.<br /> <br /> I would not wish the experiences I've had on anyone. Yet, sometimes I wish I could, if only for a moment, so that people could intuitively understand how ridiculous it is to compare the accusation of racism with racism itself.<br /> <br /> <b>It's a lot like people reacting so strongly to a show because it's entitled Dear White People</b>].</div> </div> </div> </div> On the nose.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T23:43:00-07:00","id":1086494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086483#post1086483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not wish the experiences I've had on anyone. Yet, sometimes I wish I could, if only for a moment, so that people could intuitively understand how ridiculous it is to compare the accusation of racism with racism itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>reminds me of this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/ZPDpcYEdiOg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/ZPDpcYEdiOg\" target=\"_blank\"> YouTube </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/ZPDpcYEdiOg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/embed/ZPDpcYEdiOg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T06:37:16-07:00","id":1086586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086420#post1086420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it is not just that the n-word is not something that white people can say, it is something that no one who isn't black should say, that includes non-black poc, and the idea that his guy didnt know the meaning or the implication behind the word is a bit ludicrous, unless he was an exceptionally ignorant person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not everyone from other countries has a strong grasp on US history and American slang. When he first got over here, he didn't know the history behind the n-word and didn't realize it referred to black people specifically. He thought it was a synonym for criminal and that it equally applied to everybody regardless of race, because his only context with ever having heard the word was in rap music or a few action movies, where people casually used the word and nobody cared.<br /> <br /> There were lots of slang words he had trouble dealing with. Like the time he tells me, &quot;I almost punched this black kid today. He came up and called me a dog! But then it seems everyone calls each other dogs. Why do people do that? Back in my country, if you call someone a dog, you would get your ass kicked so hard.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well yeah, it's okay to call someone a dog. Nobody gets mad.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;So I can just call a person a dog? I can just say, 'Hey, dog,' and he would not care?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well no, if you call someone a dog you should change the stress of the word to dawg and do it in a friendly way. &quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;So just call someone a dog in a friendly way?&quot; He started laughing so hard I thought he was going to fall over.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or with the word 'nigga.' He was using that word that and I had to tell him it was short for the n-word and he couldn't say it.<br /> <br /> &quot;But everyone says it at school! The black people say it to white people. The white people say to black people. The Mexicans say it to everyone! How can it be offensive?&quot;<br /> <br /> I explained the history and how it derived from the n-word and that it wasn't something that anyone should say, even if it seemed like everyone said it.<br /> <br /> So then he went to school the next day and asked some of the black kids there and they said that maybe a <i>few</i> people would find it offensive, but whatever, he (and everyone else) could say it at school and nobody would care. Basically they told him that while the full n-word was offensive, this one was not, that black people had &quot;taken this word back&quot; so that's why it was okay if people, even white people used it. While the other version of the word was offensive, this was just a friendly greeting.<br /> <br /> But then they followed it up by telling him not everyone saw it the same way and if he said it to the wrong person in the wrong place, he might get his ass kicked, so he should only say it at school.<br /> <br /> &quot;So it's okay to say this word in one place, and everyone says it, but if I were to say it somewhere else I could get my ass kicked? I'm really glad I figured that it out before something like that happened.&quot; He just shook his head.<br /> <br /> So yeah, lots of confusion over what's fine to say, what's not fine to say, where it's okay to say and who it's okay to say to, and how something can be offensive if you stress the word one way or not the other way. Plus he soon realized that not everyone was even on the same page when it came to these things, which often made it even more confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-02-2017, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:37:47-07:00","id":1086626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086586#post1086586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the lesson to take away from this is &quot;never use anyone else's slang without doing cultural studies first.&quot; <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:56:57-07:00","id":1086634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086626#post1086626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the lesson to take away from this is &quot;never use anyone else's slang without doing cultural studies first.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, slang is really confusing. Especially when there's not an easy way to immediately know which words are slang words and which aren't, and when a word is being used as slang and when it's being used normally, until you're pretty comfortable with casual conversations in that language. Which really takes at least a few months of immersion before you get that familiar. Plus it's often necessary to have people with a good grasp of the culture and the language who can explain how everything works to you, and help work you through linguistic pitfalls you probably don't even know exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-02-2017, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T08:48:24-07:00","id":1086655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086015#post1086015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But even after he left he told me he still found many of the ideas of race in America, and what's acceptable and what isn't acceptable, and who can say something and who can't say something to be incredibly confusing and often arbitrary. We had some interesting conversations though, and it really made me sit down and spend some time thinking about race in a way that I probably never would have done otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had similar conversation with people from outside the States looking in on what looks like a really strange, contorted, and arbitrary set of cultural mores with regards to race. The best answer I've been able to give is that our racial hangups <i>are</i> strange, contorted, and arbitrary because the systems of strange, contorted, and arbitrary racial oppression existed in this country for longer than they have (arguably) not existed, and trying to unbend that warped culture creates all sorts of bumps, kinks, and splinters of its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T09:11:16-07:00","id":1086662,"title":"","content":"This video seems relevant, from about 2:30 to 5:00.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/tGUKox8ewUM\" data-code=\"tGUKox8ewUM\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/tGUKox8ewUM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T10:04:46-07:00","id":1086683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086655#post1086655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had similar conversation with people from outside the States looking in on what looks like a really strange, contorted, and arbitrary set of cultural mores with regards to race. The best answer I've been able to give is that our racial hangups <i>are</i> strange, contorted, and arbitrary because the systems of strange, contorted, and arbitrary racial oppression existed in this country for longer than they have (arguably) not existed, and trying to unbend that warped culture creates all sorts of bumps, kinks, and splinters of its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>purely anecdotal comment, but I remember back in high school in Canada about 25 years ago we had to read &quot;To Kill a Mockingbird&quot;. I (and the rest of the class) largely missed large chunks of the white/black core racial elements in the book and had to have them pointed out to us by the teacher.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say Canada doesn't have racism or intolerance (it has a lot especially in some areas), just that without a depth of exposure to the whole way it works in the US, it's actually somewhat difficult to understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T10:17:38-07:00","id":1086689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086427#post1086427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem with this is not that it isn't true, but how often those kind of reasoning focuses only on what white people do, while in reality, everyone does that, every ethnicity has biases toward their own and against others.<br /> <br /> Often, it's resulting in demonizing white people, while idolizing other races and cultures. No, the &quot;others did the same&quot; isn't a redeemer for anything, I said that in an older thread and I still think that, but accentuating only one side of the things is also discrimination.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A problem I see with a lot of people trying to understand socially progressive rhetoric is that <i>fair </i>doesn't mean <i>equal</i>. Sometimes people assume that all categories in a set have to be treated evenly and the same; and, that's <i>fair</i>.<br /> <br /> But that's not always true, because of outside factors.<br /> <br /> For example, there's a lot of college scholarships available only to non-white people. That's not an even distribution, but it is fair, because non-white people also tend to suffer from higher levels of poverty and economic trouble because a wide range of subtle factors in how our society is structured. <br /> <br /> The reason I bring this is because of why people focus more on the biases of white people vs the biases of non-white people. Because white people have a much greater hold on Western or US society and the trajectory there-of than any other group. There's simply more of them; and, some of them have build for themselves power structures that give them an advantage to maintaining that control.<br /> <br /> So their biases are far more likely to work their way into reality; and, to become part of the framework of our society and culture than of other groups. Even if every single black person wanted to discriminate against white people, there simply aren't enough of them, nor do they have the same strangle hold on our society.<br /> <br /> @ Are all white people racist?<br /> <br /> I don't think all white people are racist, but a strong minority of them are. Most of the rest are just sort of.. race apathetic. They don't care at all about racial issues, or about the struggles that minority groups go through; and, react strongly when someone tries to bring it up to them. &quot;Why should I care about this,&quot; they say, or &quot;I've never experienced this, so it can't be that much of a problem.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T10:31:28-07:00","id":1086699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086683#post1086683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">purely anecdotal comment, but I remember back in high school in Canada about 25 years ago we had to read &quot;To Kill a Mockingbird&quot;. I (and the rest of the class) largely missed large chunks of the white/black core racial elements in the book and had to have them pointed out to us by the teacher.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say Canada doesn't have racism or intolerance (it has a lot especially in some areas), just that without a depth of exposure to the whole way it works in the US, it's actually somewhat difficult to understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Racism beyond the instinctual 'tribe mind' look is a learned behavior. Most learn it from their parents, or friends or other family growing up, some later in life by speakers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T10:45:53-07:00","id":1086707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086662#post1086662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This video seems relevant, from about 2:30 to 5:00.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/tGUKox8ewUM\" data-code=\"tGUKox8ewUM\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/tGUKox8ewUM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, that was interesting.<br /> <br /> Another thing I thought about yesterday is your (ie. Americans) connection to religions, specifically Christianity. Like, you know, you have this whole social justice issue and picture yourself as the home of progressive thinking, but effectively every public officer, even the president and everyone in the court of law taking oaths on the Bible. Honestly, it's so strange to me, I can't even convey how much. For example, I could never, ever imagine a nation-wide hysteria in Europe the infamous D&amp;D satanic panic was over there. It's just mind-boggling how it can happened in the second half of the 20th century, in a country which supposedly is the epitome of freedom? It's also telling and quite funny and sad at the same time that among the most fervent critics of the recent Pope are the American Christians.<br /> <br /> Like there is literally two US, one, the quite religious US mostly in rural and suburban regions and then the progressive-liberal metropolitan areas and both are a bit (or quite) extreme in irreconcilability. I know it's an oversimplification, and might be totally wrong but I see from here a very sharp and convoluted division. Naturally this kind of thing exist here too, but, aside from the truly extreme minority we handle it more... I don't know, on the basis of live and let live. We just don't want to convert or eliminate each other constantly, for the most part.<br /> <br /> Also, I thought about asking what is exactly the &quot;white privilege&quot; (since some people handle it as the ultimate argument-ender) and how it manifests nowadays? Again, I'm from Hungary and, while we have problems of our own, with the integration of the Roma communities, we never had the whole imperialism/colonialism/slavery thing, although we had actual Nazism (and communism, which was every bit as bad and lasted waaay longer), so our baselines differ. I don't believe we really have a privilege of any kind (even in comparison to the Roma, it's just much more complex than that) and Hungarian minorities are also quite persecuted in neighbor states.<br /> <br /> Also-also, what are the real problems of poc communities in the US and how it could be addressed? If any one of you feel the inclination, feel free to write about it, I'd appreciate it, since it's an interesting discussion, but I think I'm getting a bit out of depth here, language-wise, to really discuss that eloquently and/or it'd take so much time I don't really want to spend on it right now. Alternatively, I'd like to read articles on it, but preferably moderate, sensible and honest ones, not the propaganda of either side (although I know, google is just a click away, but since a lot of you already quite keen on the topic...).<br /> <br /> Things that came into my mind:<br /> <br /> - the US' tendency toward political dynasties and the lack of apparent black politicians on the national level (despite Obama)<br /> - poverty and it's derivatives, like under-educatedness, higher crime rates, etc.<br /> - the different handling of white and black people in police dispatches. Is it likely that a black person would get a higher level of penalty for the exact same crime in the court? Also, why police officers, even poc ones tend to react more harshly to black people, which led to some tragic events? My initial suspect is the ingrained reflexes going back to the past decades, which seen more gang violence and overall crime and it connects to the former point (poverty), but all of this could be the result of pop-culture stereotypes. <br /> <br /> And in the end: what white people are exactly doing to maintain the problems? How 'racism' works in everyday life, to, as some of you said, &quot;to maintain privilege and the status quo&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T10:56:31-07:00","id":1086709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086707#post1086707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I thought about asking what is exactly the &quot;white privilege&quot; (since some people handle it as the ultimate argument-ender) and how it manifests nowadays?</div> </div> </div> </div>So white privilege - basically different people are treated in different ways. White people in the US don't have to really worry about stop and frisk police policies. White people don't have to worry as much about living in ghettos. White-heavy schools tend to have more funding and support. People with white names often have an easier time getting hired for jobs. <br /> <br /> There are a lot of ways, some really small, some not so small, in which being a white person gives someone an advantage. White privilege simply recognizes that all of these little things, which white people often take for granted, add up to a lot over the course of someone's life. If like is like a 100 meter dash, then it's like white people get to start 5 meters ahead of everyone else. It's an advantage, but that's not to say that blacks and other members of minorities can't succeed, or that white people can't fail. Just that being a white person in America is easier in a lot of really small (and occasionally large) ways.<br /> <br /> Also, native Hungarians are surely privileged over Roma, yes? Roma face a lot of prejudices and issues in Hungary that non-Roma don't face. While you might not call it &quot;white privilege&quot; in Hungary, you could call it &quot;native privilege.&quot; And this is true in many nations, where the native population faces advantages over immigrants or people who don't match up the predominant ethnic or racial characteristics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T11:14:01-07:00","id":1086717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086689#post1086689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A problem I see with a lot of people trying to understand socially progressive rhetoric is that <i>fair </i>doesn't mean <i>equal</i>. Sometimes people assume that all categories in a set have to be treated evenly and the same; and, that's <i>fair</i>.<br /> <br /> But that's not always true, because of outside factors.<br /> <br /> For example, there's a lot of college scholarships available only to non-white people. That's not an even distribution, but it is fair, because non-white people also tend to suffer from higher levels of poverty and economic trouble because a wide range of subtle factors in how our society is structured.<br /> <br /> The reason I bring this is because of why people focus more on the biases of white people vs the biases of non-white people. Because white people have a much greater hold on Western or US society and the trajectory there-of than any other group. There's simply more of them; and, some of them have build for themselves power structures that give them an advantage to maintaining that control.<br /> <br /> So their biases are far more likely to work their way into reality; and, to become part of the framework of our society and culture than of other groups. Even if every single black person wanted to discriminate against white people, there simply aren't enough of them, nor do they have the same strangle hold on our society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are different things in my mind. Supporting people, who came from harder upbringings is good, although I won't do its majority based on race, but simply on need, but sometimes, targetin specific groups with support is indeed justifiable.<br /> <br /> But giving a group of people more slack, while demonizing other people? Sorry, but no, I can't stand behind that, regardless of who is doing that tho whom. Honestly, &quot;only white people could be racists&quot; and &quot;white people gaining more leeway from law enforcement&quot; (I mean in the case it's really happening, not the accusation of it) is the exact same kind of bullsh*t. I don't believe large-scale favoritism will lead to anything good, it just swings the pendulum back and forth and essentially guarantees that the biases and resentment will remain between the groups.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> @ Are all white people racist?<br /> <br /> I don't think all white people are racist, but a strong minority of them are. </div> </div> </div>Probably. I know some, there are persons like that everywhere, but indeed it's a minority, but a very vocal one. I suspect, just like with the extreme left.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of the rest are just sort of.. race apathetic. They don't care at all about racial issues, or about the struggles that minority groups go through; and, react strongly when someone tries to bring it up to them. &quot;Why should I care about this,&quot; they say, or &quot;I've never experienced this, so it can't be that much of a problem.&quot; </div> </div> </div>It's not as much as &quot;don't caring&quot;, it's more like looking at people as people, as persons and handling them as such, instead of looking for the racial (or other social and identity) issues in everything and every time. That's not denial, just not over-focusedness. I might add, I think it's somewhat on point idea in the video Charlaquin linked that you're <i>really </i>focused on identity politics. Like you'd feel the urge to constantly defend and justify your identities and the need for a myriad of labels, etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T11:39:21-07:00","id":1086722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086709#post1086709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So white privilege - basically different people are treated in different ways. White people in the US don't have to really worry about stop and frisk police policies. White people don't have to worry as much about living in ghettos. White-heavy schools tend to have more funding and support. People with white names often have an easier time getting hired for jobs.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of ways, some really small, some not so small, in which being a white person gives someone an advantage. White privilege simply recognizes that all of these little things, which white people often take for granted, add up to a lot over the course of someone's life. If like is like a 100 meter dash, then it's like white people get to start 5 meters ahead of everyone else. It's an advantage, but that's not to say that blacks and other members of minorities can't succeed, or that white people can't fail. Just that being a white person in America is easier in a lot of really small (and occasionally large) ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'd think on that, thanks!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, native Hungarians are surely privileged over Roma, yes? Roma face a lot of prejudices and issues in Hungary that non-Roma don't face. While you might not call it &quot;white privilege&quot; in Hungary, you could call it &quot;native privilege.&quot; And this is true in many nations, where the native population faces advantages over immigrants or people who don't match up the predominant ethnic or racial characteristics. </div> </div> </div>As I said, it's not that simple. According to Roma intellectuals, their biggest problem is their politicians and all the implications of being in poverty, but also some of the cultural customs. I suspect on these parts, it's quite similar to the problems of black communities over there.<br /> <br /> Still, most people don't have problems with the Roma, because of skin color, but because of how they're frequently acting and their lifestyles and they don't really have problems with the integrated communities and families. Nobody wants to be around jerks, bullies and criminals and yes it hurts Roma who aren't like that a LOT.<br /> <br /> It's really a chicken and egg question: yes, there are certain prejudices against the Roma, but it didn't come from slavery, but from their different culture (which is... not the most compatible with the majority's) and now the two thing strengthening each other in a toxic way and both sides are equally guilty that the situation isn't really changing. You can't really point on just one group as guilty as in the US.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T11:57:39-07:00","id":1086729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086722#post1086722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, most people don't have problems with the Roma, because of skin color, but because of how they're frequently acting and their lifestyles and they don't really have problems with the integrated communities and families. Nobody wants to be around jerks, bullies and criminals and yes it hurts Roma who aren't like that a LOT.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but keep in mind that privilege can take many forms. You can have racial privilege, cultural privilege, economic privilege, sex/gender privilege, etc.<br /> <br /> For example, imagine two people, one born to a poor Roma family and one born to an ethnic Hungarian whose father owns a business worth $100 million dollars. Even if they have the same goals in life (say, both of them want to be chemical engineers) and both of them work just as hard, the Roma is going to have a much harder time being successful because he will have to deal with his own cultural problems, plus he'll have deal to prejudices from other people who look down on him because he's Roma.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the ethnic Hungarian won't have to deal with any of those disadvantages. Thanks to his ethnic and cultural privilege (being able to fit in with the majority culture) he will have an advantage in his life. Then you include his economic and education privileges (his family is very wealthy and his father hires the best tutors for him and makes sure he gets into the best school in the country) and you can see the Roma is going to have to work much, much harder to accomplish the same thing as the ethnic Hungarian.<br /> <br /> Even just two equally poor people, an ethnic Hungarian and a Roma, the ethnic Hungarian would have an easier time of getting ahead in society - he wouldn't have to deal with slurs, or prejudice, or people assuming he's a criminal or a bully or a thief just because of his race. It's not <i>exactly</i> the same but it is similar to blacks and whites in the US, where blacks are often the victims of stereotypes and have to work harder than whites to accomplish the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T12:12:29-07:00","id":1086732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086717#post1086717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But giving a group of people more slack, while demonizing other people? Sorry, but no, I can't stand behind that, regardless of who is doing that tho whom. Honestly, &quot;only white people could be racists&quot; and &quot;white people gaining more leeway from law enforcement&quot; (I mean in the case it's really happening, not the accusation of it) is the exact same kind of bullsh*t. I don't believe large-scale favoritism will lead to anything good, it just swings the pendulum back and forth and essentially guarantees that the biases and resentment will remain between the groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you draw the line? What policy could you write, what language could you use, that would help to elevate people who have historically been on the receiving end of oppressive treatment <i>without</i> condemning the acts of the oppressors? <br /> <br /> Just last night, there was a protest in New Orleans about the removal of a statue of Jefferson Davis. Scores of protesters surrounded the statue, shouting at counter-protesters and preventing the statue from coming down. I expect most of those people did not think of themselves as racists so much as supporters of states' rights and the like. I expect they took umbrage at the idea that Davis was, in some way, a champion of slavers and slavery, and that keeping up a monument to him might promote slavers and slavery in addition to states' rights. <br /> <br /> How do you reconcile those beliefs?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086717#post1086717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not as much as &quot;don't caring&quot;, it's more like looking at people as people, as persons and handling them as such, instead of looking for the racial (or other social and identity) issues in everything and every time. That's not denial, just not over-focusedness.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's very, very fine line between &quot;looking at people as people&quot; and &quot;being oblivious to or willfully ignoring real social problems.&quot;<br /> <br /> My experience with people who &quot;don't think about race&quot; or &quot;don't see race&quot; has tended towards the latter. Many white privileged people seem to assume that minorities have all the same privileges they have; and if minorities are unable to succeed despite having those privileges, it must be a sign of a personal failing rather than external factors dragging them down. This is especially true for people who think of themselves as &quot;self-made&quot;, and believe that every individual makes their own fate. <br /> <br /> I know this to be true, because I used to do it too. I don't feel guilt or shame for being a beneficiary of a system that oppresses certain people, but that doesn't mean I don't feel responsible. As a participant in this society, I have the ability to try to steer things in a more positive direction - through my votes, through my interactions with other people, and through my publications. If I don't do that, then I become an accomplice to the oppressors, something for which I <i>should</i> feel shame and guilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T12:47:38-07:00","id":1086746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086717#post1086717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But giving a group of people more slack, while demonizing other people? Sorry, but no, I can't stand behind that, regardless of who is doing that tho whom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you realize that that's how things are right now? Some people are demonized while other groups are given more slack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T12:48:13-07:00","id":1086747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086729#post1086729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, but keep in mind that privilege can take many forms. You can have racial privilege, cultural privilege, economic privilege, sex/gender privilege, etc.<br /> <br /> For example, imagine two people, one born to a poor Roma family and one born to an ethnic Hungarian whose father owns a business worth $100 million dollars. Even if they have the same goals in life (say, both of them want to be chemical engineers) and both of them work just as hard, the Roma is going to have a much harder time being successful because he will have to deal with his own cultural problems, plus he'll have deal to prejudices from other people who look down on him because he's Roma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, most of us, not-rich people would have just as hard a time. If people are seeing that you work hard and being polite and all-in-all an okay person, most of us won't care about skin color.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meanwhile the ethnic Hungarian won't have to deal with any of those disadvantages. Thanks to his ethnic and cultural privilege (being able to fit in with the majority culture) he will have an advantage in his life. </div> </div> </div>Yes, because he's rich, he won't. Honestly, fitting in isn't that hard. Most of us have Roma friends. The Roma are here, I don't know exactly since which century, but for many. We're accustomed to each other and as far as I know, we never had things like &quot;you can't sit in the front of the bus&quot;, or &quot;white-only shop&quot;. Maybe during the Nazi regime, I don't know. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then you include his economic and education privileges </div> </div> </div>Those are much more important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (his family is very wealthy and his father hires the best tutors for him and makes sure he gets into the best school in the country) and you can see the Roma is going to have to work much, much harder to accomplish the same thing as the ethnic Hungarian. </div> </div> </div>First of, most of us attends to the same state schools and we're going to the same classes. The rich fellow might have personal teachers or going to a private school, but again, he'd have the same advantage over the 98% of us.<br /> <br /> Mostly, the Roma would have to work harder, because their culture just doesn't support education (and integration), they have to go against the flow, possible their own family, if they aren't from the already middle-class, or intellectual families. If they're want to do it, most people, teachers, etc. are quite willing to support them. Obviously, it's not all nice and pink here we have bad seeds too, but honestly, most of us would be happy to see their situation changing, partly, because it costs us a lot of money.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even just two equally poor people, an ethnic Hungarian and a Roma, the ethnic Hungarian would have an easier time of getting ahead in society - he wouldn't have to deal with slurs, or prejudice, </div> </div> </div>Maybe. Not necessarily. Likely depending on the career path.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or people assuming he's a criminal or a bully or a thief just because of his race. </div> </div> </div>They won't if he won't act like that, but I admit, people could be wary at first. You won't find a family in my town where at least one member didn't get attacked/robbed by Roma, or their things stolen or their houses broken in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not <i>exactly</i> the same but it is similar to blacks and whites in the US, where blacks are often the victims of stereotypes and have to work harder than whites to accomplish the same thing. </div> </div> </div>The singificant difference is that you're saying that blacks are the victims of this prejudice and their situation is mostly due to white people. In the case of the Roma, among the cases of their situation, you'd find as many, or more internal factors as external ones and the two constantly plays into each other. It's more akin to the situation of Muslim minorities in European cities and in those cases, really, the biggest problem is the existence of parallel societies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T13:05:42-07:00","id":1086753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086732#post1086732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do you draw the line? What policy could you write, what language could you use, that would help to elevate people who have historically been on the receiving end of oppressive treatment <i>without</i> condemning the acts of the oppressors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, just treating everyone equally? If someone committed a crime, then punish it equally? If someone get a degree, employ them equally?<br /> <br /> And you can condemn the acts of oppressors. I don't think anyone said that slavery was okay. I just don't think most people nowadays count as &quot;oppressors&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just last night, there was a protest in New Orleans about the removal of a statue of Jefferson Davis. Scores of protesters surrounded the statue, shouting at counter-protesters and preventing the statue from coming down. I expect most of those people did not think of themselves as racists so much as supporters of states' rights and the like. I expect they took umbrage at the idea that Davis was, in some way, a champion of slavers and slavery, and that keeping up a monument to him might promote slavers and slavery in addition to states' rights.<br /> <br /> How do you reconcile those beliefs? </div> </div> </div>Simply put, I can disagree with the model of the statue, even hate what he stood for, but it's part of history. I don't agree, on principle, with the communist philosophy of erasing the past.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's very, very fine line between &quot;looking at people as people&quot; and &quot;being oblivious to or willfully ignoring real social problems.&quot;<br /> <br /> My experience with people who &quot;don't think about race&quot; or &quot;don't see race&quot; has tended towards the latter. Many white privileged people seem to assume that minorities have all the same privileges they have; and if minorities are unable to succeed despite having those privileges, it must be a sign of a personal failing rather than external factors dragging them down. This is especially true for people who think of themselves as &quot;self-made&quot;, and believe that every individual makes their own fate. </div> </div> </div>I feel you're drawing a line between victims and oppressors and I just think those things are tend to be more nuanced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086746#post1086746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you realize that that's how things are right now? Some people are demonized while other groups are given more slack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, we just don't necessarily speaking about the same groups. However, demonizing the other side is something everyone does, so we're probably both right, at least I know I'd agree that minorities are got to be demonized, sadly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T13:12:48-07:00","id":1086754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086722#post1086722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really a chicken and egg question: yes, there are certain prejudices against the Roma, but it didn't come from slavery, but from their different culture (which is... not the most compatible with the majority's) and now the two thing strengthening each other in a toxic way and both sides are equally guilty that the situation isn't really changing. You can't really point on just one group as guilty as in the US.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite fair to place biases against the Roma solely at their feet. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antiziganism\" target=\"_blank\">A lot of it came from centuries of blood libel and scapegoating them, going as far back as the 1300s</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T13:39:11-07:00","id":1086765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086754#post1086754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not quite fair to place biases against the Roma solely at their feet. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antiziganism\" target=\"_blank\">A lot of it came from centuries of blood libel and scapegoating them, going as far back as the 1300s</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I especially didn't placed it solely at their feet (but it might be that I just planned to wrote it). It's a mess, honestly, it originated in cultural differences, which resulted in bad acts on both sides, which resulted in more biases, then more acts, etc. In situations like this, no one is really innocent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T14:22:07-07:00","id":1086787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086753#post1086753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, I can disagree with the model of the statue, even hate what he stood for, but it's part of history. I don't agree, on principle, with the communist philosophy of erasing the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where it's clear to me that you're approaching this with a set of misunderstandings that I'm not sure how to address.<br /> <br /> The people defending these statues are the ones erasing the past. They are the ones who tell their children that Jefferson Davis, the president of the Confederacy, fought for state's rights, not for enslavement. Not all monuments are created equal. If a plaque (like the one my advisor showed me a little while back) talks about a location as a place where &quot;slaves were sold&quot; and Andrew Jackson planned the Battle of New Orleans, that plaque erases history, like the hundreds of members of indigenous nations that Jackson slaughtered during the conflict. The monuments you are defending reinforce lies and propaganda that erase the past every single day. Tours at many plantations in the south--where I'm from, by the way--often talk about everything except for the fact that they were built by enslaved men and women. You can use anti-communist buzz words all you'd like, but leftists are not the ones erasing the past in this equation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T14:46:48-07:00","id":1086805,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086747#post1086747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly, the Roma would have to work harder, because their culture just doesn't support education (and integration), they have to go against the flow, possible their own family, if they aren't from the already middle-class, or intellectual families. If they're want to do it, most people, teachers, etc. are quite willing to support them. Obviously, it's not all nice and pink here we have bad seeds too, but honestly, most of us would be happy to see their situation changing, partly, because it costs us a lot of money.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is literally ethnic privilege. You, as a person, are lucky you were not born as a Roma. They have a culture that is, in many respects, poisonous and hurts their own members (I would say the same thing about African-American culture and their idolization of gangsters, crime-positive beliefs, blatant sexist and anti-feminist beliefs, etc). And, the greater Hungarian society does not look kindly on Roma, and they often face other problems involving Hungarian society that ethnic Hungarians do not face. Not being born into Roma culture or having the problems that come with being Roma is one of the advantages that you were born with.<br /> <br /> &quot;Checking your privilege&quot; is about recognizing the fact that you were born in a better position - perhaps economically, perhaps ethnically, perhaps based off your sex and gender, than other people were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T14:50:11-07:00","id":1086806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086753#post1086753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe, just treating everyone equally? If someone committed a crime, then punish it equally? If someone get a degree, employ them equally?<br /> <br /> And you can condemn the acts of oppressors. I don't think anyone said that slavery was okay. I just don't think most people nowadays count as &quot;oppressors&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me rephrase the question. I asked how you would give some people who are historically oppressed a boost, <i>and </i> condemn others who will not punish crimes or employ people equally, without anyone crying &quot;favoritism&quot; or &quot;demonization&quot;? How would you achieve that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086753#post1086753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, I can disagree with the model of the statue, even hate what he stood for, but it's part of history. I don't agree, on principle, with the communist philosophy of erasing the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody's arguing that Davis' name should be erased from the history books. But when you put someone on a literal pedestal, that is equivalent to endorsing their values. What, then, if those values are anathema to you?<br /> <br /> I should add that statue was put up in 1908, when Davis was long dead but Jim Crow laws were at their peak. In 1910, less than 0.5% of eligible black men in Louisiana were registered to vote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086753#post1086753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel you're drawing a line between victims and oppressors and I just think those things are tend to be more nuanced.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bMost people may not count as <i>intentional </i>oppressors. Unfortunately, this is an issue where ignorance or refusal to take a position makes somebody a tacit supporter of the status quo. On the other hand, just being aware of history and consciously trying to correct for it can make a tremendous difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T14:54:55-07:00","id":1086809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086753#post1086753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, I can disagree with the model of the statue, even hate what he stood for, but it's part of history. I don't agree, on principle, with the communist philosophy of erasing the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adolf Hitler and Joseph Stalin deserve to be remembered in history. But they don't deserve to have giant statues of themselves sitting around towns.<br /> <br /> That said, I tend to also be a bit weary of taking down historical monuments. Rather, I think the best thing to do is to erect a new monument to give a different meaning to the older one. Sometimes you can change the venue of a statue to alter its meaning. One of the best recent examples is of the way the Fearless Girl statue changed the meaning of the Charging Bull statue, which was originally meant as a positive business statue but with the Fearless Girl standing in contrast, suddenly the Charging Bull took on tones of patriarchy and male dominance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.gannett-cdn.com/-mm-/22ee2d162bcf25260f5af4996cf8607d1b1b6755/c=240-0-5275-3786&amp;r=x404&amp;c=534x401/local/-/media/2017/03/26/USATODAY/USATODAY/636261668882296548-AP-FEARLESS-GIRL-WALL-STREET-89821798.JPG\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I feel that creating a new statue to give the older statue or monument context and show <i>why it is bad</i> is much better than tearing those statues down. Keep up the statue of the racist SOB, but put up another statue memorializing the people who were hurt by them to give context and meaning to what happened. &quot;This is racist SOB who did <i>this. </i>Do not forget what happened and who did it,&quot; is much better than just tearing things down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T14:58:03-07:00","id":1086811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086809#post1086809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel that creating a new statue to give the older statue or monument context and show <i>why it is bad</i> is much better than tearing those statues down. Keep up the statue of the racist SOB, but put up another statue memorializing the people who were hurt by them to give context and meaning to what happened. &quot;This is racist SOB who did <i>this</i>,&quot; is much better than just tearing things down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would totally support this as well, and some places have done it. <br /> <br /> Right or wrong, the removal of Confederate monuments equates the experience to the Holocaust in a lot of ways. It draws a comparison, as you did initially, to the banning of the display of Nazi paraphernalia, and the erection of stumbling stones throughout Europe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T15:01:22-07:00","id":1086813,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Andrew Jackson, by the way, these thoughts from Civil War historians are interesting:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.com/news/world-us-canada-39723586\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_news/1200/cpsprodpb/79B1/production/_95835113_trump_jackson.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.com/news/world-us-canada-39723586\" target=\"_blank\"> Civil War historians take on Trump </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.com/news/world-us-canada-39723586\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.bbc.com/news/world-us-canada-39723586 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Three prominent historians try to break down the president's comments on Andrew Jackson and war. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T15:09:23-07:00","id":1086821,"title":"","content":"Reading that interview it seemed like Trump believes the abolition of slavery was equivalent to the government regulations regarding big business that he's so against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T15:19:06-07:00","id":1086828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086821#post1086821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading that interview it seemed like Trump believes the abolition of slavery was equivalent to the government regulations regarding big business that he's so against.</div> </div> </div> </div>He thinks there could have been a compromise, which is alarming. And I think they're right that he's talking about the wrong Andrew. Which, you know, one white guy named Andrew Jackson, one white guy named Andrew Johnson. I'm not even being a little bit facetious, I can understand why someone would get confused if it's not their strong suit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T16:30:04-07:00","id":1086860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086828#post1086828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He thinks there could have been a compromise, which is alarming. And I think they're right that he's talking about the wrong Andrew. Which, you know, one white guy named Andrew Jackson, one white guy named Andrew Johnson. I'm not even being a little bit facetious, I can understand why someone would get confused if it's not their strong suit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No he's not, he idolizes Jackson as a &quot;strong&quot; leader uplifted by a populist revolution against &quot;elites&quot;. He meant Jackson.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T16:35:06-07:00","id":1086864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086753#post1086753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Simply put, I can disagree with the model of the statue, even hate what he stood for, but it's part of history. I don't agree, on principle, with the communist philosophy of erasing the past.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>THe only people erasing the past are the people editing history to make the Confederates and those who honor them anything but racist terrorists and terrorist-sympathizers. Taking down of a statue from the public square is not &quot;erasing the past&quot; and not &quot;Communism&quot; - unless you're going to accuse oppressed Eastern Europeans who pulled down statues of Lenin after the fall of the Soviet Union of being Communists unjustly erasing the past.<br /> <br /> The history should be remembered. Most removed statues like this are put in museums.<br /> <br /> The people who want to ignore the fact that the popular &quot;Confederate Flag&quot; was only popularized by the KKK in the 1920s, and then was put up by Southern state governments to protest desegregation in the 60s, are clearly not the people who believe in remembering history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-02-2017, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T16:37:41-07:00","id":1086868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086860#post1086860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No he's not, he idolizes Jackson as a &amp;quot;strong&amp;quot; leader uplifted by a populist revolution against &amp;quot;elites&amp;quot;. He meant Jackson.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Civil War historians in that link I posted who think he's mistakenly conflating the two have convinced me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T16:38:05-07:00","id":1086869,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'm pretty sure he meant Jackson. Jackson has a roguish backstory that would appeal to someone like Trump, who likely sees himself as some sort of lost prince-slash-hero. And like the historians pointed out, Jackson's appealing as a military man, as well. And while Trump has made some big speeches about military action, when its come down to it he's balked or fumbled at every step so far.<br /> <br /> EDIT: He may have conflated facts about the two, but I think he's primarily romanticizing Andrew Jackson there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-02-2017, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T16:41:19-07:00","id":1086872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086753#post1086753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel you're drawing a line between victims and oppressors and I just think those things are tend to be more nuanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to race in the United States, the data when it comes to employment opportunity, the criminal justice system, etc etc etc, is pretty - if you'll pardon the double-meaning - black &amp; white.<br /> <br /> There is no getting around the empirical fact that our society is still largely structured on racial inequality. The entire modern War on Drugs was consciously designed as a way to target and criminalize black men in the wake of Jim Crow's decline, for example. Color blindness in this case is just willful ignorance of the lack of the &quot;treat people equally&quot; goal you mentioned at the beginning of your post. We don't - and we don't do it specifically along lines of race, and it's only going to get solved by addressing it directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T16:47:29-07:00","id":1086874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086753#post1086753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe, just treating everyone equally? If someone committed a crime, then punish it equally? If someone get a degree, employ them equally?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we don't currently do that, and the overwhelming empirical evidence is we don't do it specifically along lines of race. How do you suggest fixing that without directly address systemic racial power structures?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T18:52:09-07:00","id":1086935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086874#post1086874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well we don't currently do that, and the overwhelming empirical evidence is we don't do it specifically along lines of race. How do you suggest fixing that without directly address systemic racial power structures?</div> </div> </div> </div>there seems to be a serious misunderstanding on the part of the poeple in oposition of equality on this discussion, as i pointed out above they think that the loss of their privliages is a form of persecution, but they also seem to have the belife at the same time that they dont have any privliages, and that they face consequences the same as everyone else and that they have acomplished what they have completely on your own.<br /> It also goes back to the response you made about the other person erasing history and then accusing people who want to stop the glorification of a man who fought for the right to own slaves as being the ones to erase history. <br /> What i see when people say, why cant everyone be just the same, or i don't see race, is that they understand the situation that is going on at least in some part, but they pretend not to becuase they want to pretend that they want things to stay the way they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T19:27:40-07:00","id":1086953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086935#post1086935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there seems to be a serious misunderstanding on the part of the poeple in oposition of equality on this discussion, as i pointed out above they think that the loss of their privliages is a form of persecution, but they also seem to have the belife at the same time that they dont have any privliages, and that they face consequences the same as everyone else and that they have acomplished what they have completely on your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that's essentially the American myth and the American ideal - that Americans &quot;pull themselves up by their own bootstraps&quot; or that they're &quot;self-made men.&quot; People who sit around saying why the deck is stacked against them are &quot;whiners.&quot; And this isn't just about race, you'll hear many Americans say the same things about white people who point towards the privileges of other, more successful citizens as the reasons for their success.<br /> <br /> This is just a deeply held, fundamental part of the American psyche. Many people have grown up, lived their whole lives and honestly believe in that ideal - that people succeed or fail ultimately on their own merits, and that if people spent less time complaining about why they couldn't get ahead, and more time working to get ahead, then they'd <i>be</i> ahead. While reality might disagree, nevertheless many Americans honestly believe it is.<br /> <br /> So often times when you discuss things like systemic power inequalities, or racial or class privilege, the response from a significant portion of the American public is to simply roll their eyes and say all of that is just jibberish - &quot;excuses&quot; made by &quot;lazy losers&quot; trying to find anyone else to blame for their lack of success, rather than simply admit they didn't work hard enough, and own up to their own failure.<br /> <br /> This is often where you run into walls with discussing such things, because these people have internalized, since childhood, the belief that work ethic trumps everything else - that a poor person with a good work ethic will be successful, and even a rich person with a poor work ethic will end up penniless. Of course, that's not entirely accurate, but that's the &quot;American Dream&quot; that has been instilled in so many people for such a long time that they have trouble imagining it's not true.<br /> <br /> For these people, they're not &quot;opposed&quot; to equality, rather they truly believe that we <i>already have</i> equality, and when someone fails it's their own fault for screwing up or not working hard enough. Trying to change that means changing the &quot;already equal&quot; playing field to give advantage to people who failed because they weren't willing to work as hard, at the expense of more successful people who are already working hard. And they view that as inherently unfair.<br /> <br /> That's why it's important to convince them that the current playing field <i>isn't</i> fair, but that runs right into the &quot;American ideal&quot; that they've spent their whole lives learning. Overturning beliefs that people have had for decades is tricky, especially when they're convinced that they'll end up being hurt if they go along with those beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T19:35:50-07:00","id":1086955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086953#post1086953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, that's essentially the American myth and the American ideal - that Americans &quot;pull themselves up by their own bootstraps&quot; or that they're &quot;self-made men.&quot; People who sit around saying why the deck is stacked against them are &quot;whiners.&quot; And this isn't just about race, you'll hear many Americans say the same things about white people who point towards the privileges of other, more successful citizens as the reasons for their success.<br /> <br /> This is just a deeply held, fundamental part of the American psyche. Many people have grown up, lived their whole lives and honestly believe in that ideal - that people succeed or fail ultimately on their own merits, and that if people spent less time complaining about why they couldn't get ahead, and more time working to get ahead, then they'd <i>be</i> ahead. While reality might disagree, nevertheless many Americans honestly believe it is.<br /> <br /> So often times when you discuss things like systemic power inequalities, or racial or class privilege, the response from a significant portion of the American public is to simply roll their eyes and say all of that is just jibberish - &quot;excuses&quot; made by &quot;lazy losers&quot; trying to find anyone else to blame for their lack of success, rather than simply admit they didn't work hard enough, and own up to their own failure.<br /> <br /> This is often where you run into walls with discussing such things, because these people have internalized, since childhood, the belief that work ethic trumps everything else - that a poor person with a good work ethic will be successful, and even a rich person with a poor work ethic will end up penniless. Of course, that's not entirely accurate, but that's the &quot;American Dream&quot; that has been instilled in so many people for such a long time that they have trouble imagining it's not true.<br /> <br /> For these people, they're not &quot;opposed&quot; to equality, rather they truly believe that we <i>already have</i> equality, and when someone fails it's their own fault for screwing up or not working hard enough. Trying to change that means changing the &quot;already equal&quot; playing field to give advantage to people who failed because they weren't willing to work as hard, at the expense of more successful people who are already working hard. And they view that as inherently unfair.<br /> <br /> That's why it's important to convince them that the current playing field <i>isn't</i> fair, but that runs right into the &quot;American ideal&quot; that they've spent their whole lives learning. Overturning beliefs that people have had for decades is tricky, especially when they're convinced that they'll end up being hurt if they go along with those beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> indoctirnation to enforce racism and classim does do quite a number on people","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T09:54:29-07:00","id":1087209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086805#post1086805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is literally ethnic privilege. You, as a person, are lucky you were not born as a Roma.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be, from that angle, yes, but I'm not sure how I'm responsible for that and how I should address that? I didn't do anything for that and also, I can't really alleviate those problems they have within their own communities. I might help, but only if they want to change too. Simply put, the oppressor/oppressed dynamics is not as applicable here as in the case of the US' post-slavery society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have a culture that is, in many respects, poisonous and hurts their own members (I would say the same thing about African-American culture and their idolization of gangsters, crime-positive beliefs, blatant sexist and anti-feminist beliefs, etc). And, the greater Hungarian society does not look kindly on Roma, and they often face other problems involving Hungarian society that ethnic Hungarians do not face. Not being born into Roma culture or having the problems that come with being Roma is one of the advantages that you were born with. </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, I thought about the same, so yes, I agree with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Checking your privilege&quot; is about recognizing the fact that you were born in a better position - perhaps economically, perhaps ethnically, perhaps based off your sex and gender, than other people were. </div> </div> </div>My problem with &quot;checking your privilege&quot; is that it is frequently used as a verbal bat, to silence opinions and closing out individuals from a discussion and even beat them into submission, just like in the case of &quot;you are just a woman, you don't understand this&quot;. And I don't like either.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086806#post1086806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me rephrase the question. I asked how you would give some people who are historically oppressed a boost, <i>and </i> condemn others who will not punish crimes or employ people equally, without anyone crying &quot;favoritism&quot; or &quot;demonization&quot;? How would you achieve that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think treating everyone equally is already the would-be norm in the West. If the law enforcement isn't doing that, there should be repercussions, since they're literally not acting according to the law. Same with employment. If you can prove that you lost your job, or don't get a job purely because of your race, that should be addressed. I know It's hard to prove that, so yes, it1s problematic. Also I don't know how it works in different branches of the economy. I don't know, how, for example a black lawyer has a harder time to getting cases?<br /> <br /> I have zero problems with boosts, like scholarships and other targeted helping, but honestly, I prefer those to be based on poverty, not color, but I could see the justification for that too in some cases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nobody's arguing that Davis' name should be erased from the history books. But when you put someone on a literal pedestal, that is equivalent to endorsing their values. What, then, if those values are anathema to you? </div> </div> </div>See below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I should add that statue was put up in 1908, when Davis was long dead but Jim Crow laws were at their peak. In 1910, less than 0.5% of eligible black men in Louisiana were registered to vote. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the fact itself, that it's there for more than a hundred years is reason enough to me to keep it, since it's part of the local's history, but again see below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bMost people may not count as <i>intentional </i>oppressors. Unfortunately, this is an issue where ignorance or refusal to take a position makes somebody a tacit supporter of the status quo. On the other hand, just being aware of history and consciously trying to correct for it can make a tremendous difference. </div> </div> </div>My opinion is that it is a little bit a &quot;if you're not with us, you're against us&quot; mentality and I'm not really agree with it. I just think it's more complicated than that, society and people are more complicated. That's why I don't like classism too. It's too much of an oversimplification of social dynamics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086809#post1086809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Adolf Hitler and Joseph Stalin deserve to be remembered in history. But they don't deserve to have giant statues of themselves sitting around towns.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they don't get any. Although, I'm not sure it's the same with this person (although I believe for the most of you here it is - and it might be, I didn't dig into the specific history, I don't have an unbound time limit), since the population really has a disagreement about it. Tearing down Stalin's statue here, in Budapest was not questioned, not for a minute. Also it was erected by the same regime itself and not a hundred years after the events. Also, I don't want to go into the whole American South thing, I'm not qualified to do that, but it's a mess of a situation in my eyes and a bit different than the Third Reich was.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> That said, I tend to also be a bit weary of taking down historical monuments. Rather, I think the best thing to do is to erect a new monument to give a different meaning to the older one. Sometimes you can change the venue of a statue to alter its meaning. One of the best recent examples is of the way the Fearless Girl statue changed the meaning of the Charging Bull statue, which was originally meant as a positive business statue but with the Fearless Girl standing in contrast, suddenly the Charging Bull took on tones of patriarchy and male dominance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <img src=\"https://www.gannett-cdn.com/-mm-/22ee2d162bcf25260f5af4996cf8607d1b1b6755/c=240-0-5275-3786&amp;r=x404&amp;c=534x401/local/-/media/2017/03/26/USATODAY/USATODAY/636261668882296548-AP-FEARLESS-GIRL-WALL-STREET-89821798.JPG\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I feel that creating a new statue to give the older statue or monument context and show <i>why it is bad</i> is much better than tearing those statues down. Keep up the statue of the racist SOB, but put up another statue memorializing the people who were hurt by them to give context and meaning to what happened. &quot;This is racist SOB who did <i>this. </i>Do not forget what happened and who did it,&quot; is much better than just tearing things down. </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, I thought along the same lines, while reading the former posts, before reading yours. If there is a consensus about that the person was a black spot in history, but the statue is a part of the landscape for a long time, then there are other, better ways to take than tearing it down. Change the context with another statue, like you said. Put a plate on the base, which is telling the whole story. Write it down in local brochures. That kind of thing.<br /> <br /> It's a bit same than with the recent squabble between our cabinet and the Central European University, founded by George Soros. Google it, if you're interested. I'm taking bsolutely the university's side on that, despite not really agreeing with some of its things, because if a right-wing party could close up schools because of ideological reasons, then the left could do the same with church-related schools and we are back to not living with each other, but trying to destroy each other and I'm seriously fed up with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1086935#post1086935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there seems to be a serious misunderstanding on the part of the poeple in oposition of equality on this discussion, as i pointed out above they think that the loss of their privliages is a form of persecution,</div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion is depending highly on the &quot;privilege&quot; we're talking about. For example, rich persons have a financial privilege, but I don't want to take away their money solely based on that they have more than I (although social net is also a thing).<br /> <br /> Also, how could I lose the &quot;privilege&quot; of not being born into awful circumstances and how could I perceive it anything but a punishment for literally just being? I have no problems with lifting up the ones who got the short end of life and I'm really not that high on the ladder (I'd say, probably, most of you are having a monetary privilege over me, just by being American), so i can understand it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but they also seem to have the belife at the same time that they dont have any privliages, and that they face consequences the same as everyone else and that they have acomplished what they have completely on your own. </div> </div> </div>That's a bit close to accusing non-minority people of not achieving anything on their own right and I won't agree with that. Also, you can't draw clear lines along the racial differences, because who had it harder is just a more complex question and things like location, upbringing, financial status and such are playing just as big, if not even bigger roles in it than purely skin color.<br /> <br /> And I do think everyone should face the same consequences.<br /> <br /> <br /> Despite all the disagreement, it was an interesting discussion, so my thanks for it! It's starting to take up just too much time to addressing everything and I think the important things were said already, so I might close my active participation in the thread for now. Again, thanks, and have a good time!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-03-2017, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T11:54:11-07:00","id":1087261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1087209#post1087209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I tend to also be a bit weary of taking down historical monuments. Rather, I think the best thing to do is to erect a new monument to give a different meaning to the older one. Sometimes you can change the venue of a statue to alter its meaning. One of the best recent examples is of the way the Fearless Girl statue changed the meaning of the Charging Bull statue, which was originally meant as a positive business statue but with the Fearless Girl standing in contrast, suddenly the Charging Bull took on tones of patriarchy and male dominance.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually a good place to touch on intent and understanding.<br /> <br /> If you ask the artist that created the charging bull statue, it was originally meant to be a symbol of the strength of the american people as a form of unauthorized gorilla art (only after it was forcefully removed did they reconsider and allow the statue to be displayed). Meanwhile the fearless girl statue on the other hand, installed just before international womens day is very specifically an advertisement for an index fund. And it's the very re-contexting that apparently has the artist of the charging pull considering removing his statue.<br /> <br /> So at what point does the intent of the piece, the intent of the author cease to matter? What history or awareness is lost by the removal? Sure, you could plaster over an offensive quote on a statue and replace it with something bland, but isn't that then simply trying to whitewash the history of things? Taking *down* the monument sends a message. It says &quot;we don't consider this acceptable, we don't consider this person a hero, this is no longer a great event.&quot; Changing the moment (to me, IMO) says more &quot;sure this happened and it was important but, uh.... we'll just edit in some additional information and suddenly someone was a good guy!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T18:35:38-07:00","id":1087443,"title":"","content":"My theory on why white people have such a problem with the concept of privilege is that it inadvertently touches on a very deeply repressed knot of insecurities a lot of white people have.<br /> <br /> First of all, under privilege theory, straight cis male white is the invisible default, which SJ activists tend to focus on the representation side of that. which is needed. But, for a large portion folks, being the invisible default, the generic brand if you will, makes it so that whiteness is more of a non-identity, an identity based on having NOTHING making you special, having no real tribe, at least for those white folks who don't come from immigrant families that held on to their traditions well. This of course, creates a sort of spiritual/identity crisis for those straight cis white men who actually think about it, so they focus on their achievements as individuals to establish their identity, but privilege theory poses a direct threat to that foundation of their self image. If they didn't build what they have, then they don't have anything, at least that is how they see it. For decades, white cismen dealt with this by creating their own substitute tribes so they did not have to rely on their own achievements &quot;goths&quot; &quot;hippies&quot; &quot;slackers&quot; AND GAMERS&quot;. The fact, the gamergate stupidity was partly because a large number of straight cis white men made gamer culture a substitute ethnic identity of sorts, it was their tribe and thus a core pillar of their self-image, so when a bunch of racial justice and feminist activists start pointing out issues in gaming and that it needs to change... well you all saw what happened.<br /> <br /> The rest of my theory on this is best explained by this <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a_yfnQPaD_E&amp;t=1367s\" target=\"_blank\">video</a><br /> <br /> <br /> The fact is, getting white people to accept privilege theory requires them to get past this identity crisis they have going on, and I have no idea how to do that (I don't agree with Shaun and Jen about class identity being the method of doing so, a tribe for the purpose I am talking about requires shared experience AND culture, class identity only has one of those).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 05-03-2017, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T19:18:17-07:00","id":1087463,"title":"","content":"I don't usually go for the youtube speakers but I think that was a good point. Part of the problem is the poor in America have, for a long, long time, believed that they're not poor. There's a quote from Steinbeck about why socialism failed here, saying that, they don't see themselves as part of a collective of lower class workers, instead 'Everyone was a temporarily embarrassed capitalist.'<br /> <br /> And like AnubisXY said it's part of the American myth that, if you're poor or whatever, you're causing it yourself and if you just pick yourself up by your bootstraps you can be a millionaire just like Trump. This, of course, ignores example after example of the rich becoming the rich by crushing the poor under their mass. Fortunately we have movies to show us how much better it is to live with family or friends and let the rich control everything.<br /> <br /> I firmly believe education is important to overcoming racism. It's a learned behavior. One can be taught truths that will bury it for good. But it's not going to be a quick fix or an easy one. Even in this show, there's no magic answers at the end that end all racism. There's people here and there mistreating blacks for the past several hundred years. And Roma since the 1300s. And Jews and Native Americans and innumerable peoples who've got the message across that they may look different or act different but they're still humans and deserve the same dignity as everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-03-2017, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T12:26:24-07:00","id":1088420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1087463#post1087463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't usually go for the youtube speakers but I think that was a good point. Part of the problem is the poor in America have, for a long, long time, believed that they're not poor. There's a quote from Steinbeck about why socialism failed here, saying that, they don't see themselves as part of a collective of lower class workers, instead 'Everyone was a temporarily embarrassed capitalist.'<br /> <br /> And like AnubisXY said it's part of the American myth that, if you're poor or whatever, you're causing it yourself and if you just pick yourself up by your bootstraps you can be a millionaire just like Trump. This, of course, ignores example after example of the rich becoming the rich by crushing the poor under their mass. Fortunately we have movies to show us how much better it is to live with family or friends and let the rich control everything.<br /> <br /> I firmly believe education is important to overcoming racism. It's a learned behavior. One can be taught truths that will bury it for good. But it's not going to be a quick fix or an easy one. Even in this show, there's no magic answers at the end that end all racism. There's people here and there mistreating blacks for the past several hundred years. And Roma since the 1300s. And Jews and Native Americans and innumerable peoples who've got the message across that they may look different or act different but they're still humans and deserve the same dignity as everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, but even the bootstraps myth is the result of white people not being able to process the fact that they don't really have a culture heritage other than domination of others and without the connection to the past and the sense of belonging to something bigger than yourself that results from having a real heritage and identity, one can quickly spiral into self loathing and nihilism, and that is where everything from cultural appropriation (stealing someone else's identity) to the nerd social fallacies such as gamergate (building an identity based on an inherently consumerist sub-cultures) predatory win at all costs capitalism (doubling down on the meritocracy myth) neoliberalism and &quot;white feminism&quot; (trying to separate oneself from whiteness and failing) and out right hatred of nonwhites (glorifying the domination of others to avoid feeling bad about it).<br /> <br /> The fact is, racism and so many of our world's other problem can't be fixed until white people resolve this identity crisis, but fuck me if I know how to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:01:45-07:00","id":1088438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088420#post1088420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly, but even the bootstraps myth is the result of white people not being able to process the fact that they don't really have a culture heritage other than domination of others and without the connection to the past and the sense of belonging to something bigger than yourself that results from having a real heritage and identity, one can quickly spiral into self loathing and nihilism, and that is where everything from cultural appropriation (stealing someone else's identity) to the nerd social fallacies such as gamergate (building an identity based on an inherently consumerist sub-cultures) predatory win at all costs capitalism (doubling down on the meritocracy myth) neoliberalism and &quot;white feminism&quot; (trying to separate oneself from whiteness and failing) and out right hatred of nonwhites (glorifying the domination of others to avoid feeling bad about it)..</div> </div> </div> </div>Two questions for y'all:<br /> 1. Are you (legally) white?<br /> 2. Have you ever felt like you didn't have an identity of value because you were &quot;white&quot;?<br /> <br /> My answers to those questions would be &quot;yes&quot; and &quot;definitely not.&quot; I've learned to take pride in being a mutt, a mix of races and cultures with the ability to pick and choose whatever I want for myself. My tribe is whoever I attach myself to, my future is what I make it to be, and my history is the combined history of everyone around me. The idea that there might be some kind of &quot;white identity&quot; I need to define and protect is confusing to me. Like, I can sort of get why that might be desirable, but only as a mechanism for separating myself from other people, and why would I want to do that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 05-05-2017, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:09:45-07:00","id":1088442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088438#post1088438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two questions for y'all:<br /> 1. Are you (legally) white?<br /> 2. Have you ever felt like you didn't have an identity of value because you were &quot;white&quot;?<br /> <br /> My answers to those questions would be &quot;yes&quot; and &quot;definitely not.&quot; I've learned to take pride in being a mutt, a mix of races and cultures with the ability to pick and choose whatever I want for myself. My tribe is whoever I attach myself to, my future is what I make it to be, and my history is the combined history of everyone around me. The idea that there might be some kind of &quot;white identity&quot; I need to define and protect is confusing to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>My answers to those questions are &quot;Yes&quot; and &quot;Also yes&quot;. Especially since I don't have a specific white ethnic group to tie myself to: I've got ancestors from all over Europe from the Mediterranean to the British Isles. Now, I don't <i>mind</i> that I lack an ethnic identity. As you say, being able to choose for myself what my ethnicity means to me is more important.<br /> <br /> But identity politics is a big deal to some people. Being able to take a label and point to it and say, &quot;That is a part of me&quot; is super important to some people. It's a foundation on which to construct an identity. And especially considering how much importance most of the world's cultures put on the Past, people can feel pressured to fit into a label, or feel &quot;wrong&quot; if they don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:39:29-07:00","id":1088463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088420#post1088420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly, but even the bootstraps myth is the result of white people not being able to process the fact that they don't really have a culture heritage other than domination of others and without the connection to the past and the sense of belonging to something bigger than yourself that results from having a real heritage and identity, one can quickly spiral into self loathing and nihilism, and that is where everything from cultural appropriation (stealing someone else's identity) to the nerd social fallacies such as gamergate (building an identity based on an inherently consumerist sub-cultures) predatory win at all costs capitalism (doubling down on the meritocracy myth) neoliberalism and &amp;quot;white feminism&amp;quot; (trying to separate oneself from whiteness and failing) and out right hatred of nonwhites (glorifying the domination of others to avoid feeling bad about it).<br /> <br /> The fact is, racism and so many of our world's other problem can't be fixed until white people resolve this identity crisis, but fuck me if I know how to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Did you seriously suggest what people don't have a cultural heritage aside from dominating over peoples? <br /> <br /> That is the most racist thing against white people I've read since the Huffington Post run the article suggesting that white people should lose the vote, but at least that had the descency to be a prank on the Huffington Post that exposed their bigotry. <br /> <br /> So Plato, Mozart, Socrates, Ed Greenwood, Stephen Hawking, the Group of Seven, Leonardo Di Vinci, Micheal Angelo, entire genras of music like country/classical/polka/rock/heavy metal/punk music, the scientific method, the modern represental Democratic system like the Parliamentary system, the invention of countless new mediums for art such as movies, television, music recording devices, countless poets and so on is no culture?!? <br /> <br /> WTF?!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T13:45:56-07:00","id":1088474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088438#post1088438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two questions for y'all:<br /> 1. Are you (legally) white?<br /> 2. Have you ever felt like you didn't have an identity of value because you were &amp;quot;white&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> My answers to those questions would be &amp;quot;yes&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;definitely not.&amp;quot; I've learned to take pride in being a mutt, a mix of races and cultures with the ability to pick and choose whatever I want for myself. My tribe is whoever I attach myself to, my future is what I make it to be, and my history is the combined history of everyone around me. The idea that there might be some kind of &amp;quot;white identity&amp;quot; I need to define and protect is confusing to me. Like, I can sort of get why that might be desirable, but only as a mechanism for separating myself from other people, and why would I want to do that?</div> </div> </div> </div> A lot of white people felt that way, until identity politics moved past a thirst for equality into activately being abusive towards white people, I personally thought of myself a Canadian and that was good enough for me, I still think race is a stupid idea. <br /> <br /> The cure for racism against minorities people isn't discrimination against white people, it's building a sense of unity and brother/sisterhood and raising all boats, not encouraging mutual antagonism, I don't even recognize the left anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T14:07:10-07:00","id":1088483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088463#post1088463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you seriously suggest what people don't have a cultural heritage aside from dominating over peoples?<br /> <br /> That is the most racist thing against white people I've read since the Huffington Post run the article suggesting that white people should lose the vote, but at least that had the descency to be a prank on the Huffington Post that exposed their bigotry.<br /> <br /> So Plato, Mozart, Socrates, Ed Greenwood, Stephen Hawking, the Group of Seven, Leonardo Di Vinci, Micheal Angelo, entire genras of music like country/classical/polka/rock/heavy metal/punk music, the scientific method, the modern represental Democratic system like the Parliamentary system, the invention of countless new mediums for art such as movies, television, music recording devices, countless poets and so on is no culture?!?<br /> <br /> WTF?!?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cultural heritage is more than that, what you are talking about is European contributions to art and science, but very little of it is anything that modern white AMERICANs have a personal historic and cultural connection to (And Greenwood is famous for making the forgotten realms, which is really just an example of the &quot;using geek culture as a substitute ethnic identity&quot; thing and only polka and classical music are purely European in ancestry. Whiteness in Europe is very different from whiteness in America because whiteness in America has been so homogenized and made an invisible default that american white people DON'T have the same sort of meaningful cultural connections to their history and community that European white people do, whiteness in America has mostly been cut off from it's various European roots and lost it's cultural heritage except for domination because domination was the only real history whiteness has in America.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T14:23:41-07:00","id":1088492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088438#post1088438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two questions for y'all:<br /> 1. Are you (legally) white?<br /> 2. Have you ever felt like you didn't have an identity of value because you were &quot;white&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and somewhat. For the latter, I've definitely felt some angst over it in the past; I'm distantly aware of some Polish Jewish heritage on my mother's side and German-Russian on my father's, but precisely zero of that heritage shines through in my life or family culture beyond how it's impacted my genetics. My family is culturally &quot;American,&quot; for as little as that means, far enough back that I've never known anything else. It makes me feel very rootless in a historical sense. My functional identity is &quot;White American,&quot; and that has ties to very little of value to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T15:17:31-07:00","id":1088513,"title":"","content":"Try asking a White American what nationality they are and see how many start with some specific European nationalities rather than starting with &quot;American&quot;. I did this experiment with some friends and only a few started with &quot;American&quot;. The majority of them (by a lot) started with Irish, Italian, German etc yet are third or fourth generation Americans. This says all I needed to know about &quot;White American&quot; identity and culture, as in there is no single unified culture. There are religious identities, regional identities but no truly definable national identity. Various groups claim to be &quot;real Americans&quot; but they are laying claim to a title that has no true definition and has multiple interpretations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T15:49:40-07:00","id":1088530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088438#post1088438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions for y'all:<br /> 1. Are you (legally) white?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically mixed race, white and Hispanic, but you'd never know it from looking at or interacting with me. My grandmother was from Puerto Rico, but married a well-off white dude and assimilated as much as she could. Her children had no real connection to their cultural heritage on her side, and less so her grandchildren. And my dad's side of the family is as Irish as they come in the US, which pretty much washed out any trace of tan I might have got from my mom.<br /> <br /> Since you ask legally though, I guess yes? Legal forms very rarely have an option that accurately represents me, since they tend to have an option for &quot;White (not Hispanic)&quot; and an option for &quot;Hispanic (not white)&quot;, and rarely have an option for mixed race.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088438#post1088438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Have you ever felt like you didn't have an identity of value because you were &quot;white&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never really thought about race as a part of identity growing up. I didn't feel a lack of identity because of it, it just never occurred to me that race played a role in identity for other people. Which is I think part of the identity crisis TYMITC was talking about. It's pretty typical for white folks to be naive to the very concept of racial identity, which is, I think, where you get ideas like treating everyone the same being equivalent to treating everyone equally.<br /> <br /> I genuinely used to think that being &quot;color blind&quot; was the way to be progressive, that all racism (and other predjudice) came from disliking people because they were different, and that it could only be ended by treating everyone as the same. <i>I</i> didn't want to be treated any differently than anyone else because of something as meaningless as the color of my skin, so it made sense to me that other people wouldn't want to be treated any differently because of the color of their skin. I never considered that others' races might have more meaning to them than the color of their skin. It clicked for me that I was looking at it the wrong way, actually related to sexuality first, and race followed. I had a teacher who was an openly gay man, who recounted a story of a coworker telling him (with good intentions), &quot;I don't see you as a gay man, I see you as a human being,&quot; to which his response was &quot;I <i>want</i> you to see me as a gay man, because <i>as</i> a gay man I don't have the same rights that you do as a straight man.&quot; (this was before gay marriage was legal in most of the country). Suddenly it dawned on me that differences existed between people, whether I acknowledged them or not, because of factors beyond my control, and that by trying to ignore those differences in the name of &quot;equality&quot; I was being complicit in those factors. And from there it wasn't a stretch to realize that this was true of other groups as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-05-2017, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T17:31:06-07:00","id":1088562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088474#post1088474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of white people felt that way, until identity politics moved past a thirst for equality into activately being abusive towards white people, I personally thought of myself a Canadian and that was good enough for me, I still think race is a stupid idea.<br /> <br /> The cure for racism against minorities people isn't discrimination against white people, it's building a sense of unity and brother/sisterhood and raising all boats, not encouraging mutual antagonism, I don't even recognize the left anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe that discrimination against white is the answer, that would just make white people hate themselves more. White people just need to learn to love themselves in a way that isn't founded on the idea that they are better than everyone else, or one trying to separate themselves from whiteness, since both of those methods of dealing with this fail badly.<br /> <br /> White people are just kind of going through an identity crisis right now and that is like... 95 percent of the current madness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2