ink":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T22:59:53-07:00","id":1088630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088438#post1088438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two questions for y'all:<br /> 1. Are you (legally) white?<br /> 2. Have you ever felt like you didn't have an identity of value because you were &quot;white&quot;?<br /> <br /> My answers to those questions would be &quot;yes&quot; and &quot;definitely not.&quot; I've learned to take pride in being a mutt, a mix of races and cultures with the ability to pick and choose whatever I want for myself. My tribe is whoever I attach myself to, my future is what I make it to be, and my history is the combined history of everyone around me. The idea that there might be some kind of &quot;white identity&quot; I need to define and protect is confusing to me. Like, I can sort of get why that might be desirable, but only as a mechanism for separating myself from other people, and why would I want to do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise on both answers. Most of the time I don't really think about either. In practical terms most of my identity tends to orient towards my political leanings and social philosophy, my atheism, my peer group and our shared interests. It doesn't help I've spent a lot of years being too Irish for English kids growing up, or too British for America,etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 05-06-2017, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T23:14:39-07:00","id":1088633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088571#post1088571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bingo. A lot of white people are terrified of no longer being seen as the default or the majority and are somehow viewing that as discrimination... without realizing that this is how they've made <i>literally everyone else feel</i> forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of white people honestly believe that racism is wrong - that treating one group of people worse than another group of people, because of their ethnicity or skin color is wrong and likewise, that treating one group of people better than another group of people because of their ethnicity or skin color, is also wrong. This is where you start running into issues with with &quot;reverse racism&quot; where groups begin passing things like racial quotas or what not, or colleges adding points to potential recruits based off of race and many white people say, &quot;Wait a second. Weren't you saying this was a problem when white people were doing it? So isn't it still a problem if other people are doing it?&quot;<br /> <br /> A lot of white people end up wondering, &quot;Well if X was unfair when white people did it, why is it fair for non-white people to do it? If something is unfair, then it's unfair regardless of who does it.&quot; This tends to leave quite a few feeling confused, or betrayed and many think, &quot;Oh I see. All the talk about an equal playing field was hypocritical. Your goal was never fairness and equality. It's just petty vindictiveness, trying to put white people on the bottom for a change.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think progressives have done a good job convincing many white people that treating people differently because of race or ethnicity is wrong, and many white people would absolutely agree with that. But those same progressives have done a rather poorer job of explaining why sometimes it <i>is</i> okay to treat people differently because or race or ethnicity.<br /> <br /> I think it falls to the people who want these kind of progressive policies to &quot;sell&quot; them and convince white people that, sometimes, giving people advantages because of their race or ethnicity <i>is</i> fair. But so far I think they've done a rather bad job of explaining why, and so many white people end up thinking a lot of these calls for equality are actually just hypocritical double-speak for trying to legalize discrimination against white people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T23:36:35-07:00","id":1088638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088633#post1088633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But those same progressives have done a rather poorer job of explaining why sometimes it <i>is</i> okay to treat people differently because or race or ethnicity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't really help that there's been plenty of people actively opposing such efforts. Trying to pin everything on progressives is a fairly insulting white-wash of the rather vile strain of conservative misinformation regarding these sorts of programs.<br /> <br /> It's hard enough to explain why someone should change their actions when there isn't someone trying to undermine you. Convincing someone to change when someone else is selling them the story that they don't need to change because there isn't really a problem to change over is exceedingly more difficult. There's a natural confirmation bias there which has been exploited repeatedly to reinforce the idea the progressive attempts to make the system more fair are &quot;reverse racism.&quot; It's not just a failure to have a good progressive sales pitch.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T00:34:38-07:00","id":1088644,"title":"","content":"I'll agree it doesn't help when you have people undermine those sorts of policies, especially members of minorities like Thomas Sowell or Ben Carson or Michelle Malkin or whomever. But fair or not, at the end of the day, if someone wants to implement Policy X, then it's ultimately on them to convince other people to go along with it since if they can't convince people to go along with it, then it's not going to happen. Now it <i>is</i> very easy to point fingers at the conservative misinformation. But realistically they're not going to stop misinforming people anytime soon, so the only options are to either do a better job of getting the real message across in an understandable way, or simply give up and accept that the conservative misinformation is here to stay.<br /> <br /> That said, I think there has been a problem with relaying these kind of ideas, even absent conservative misinformation. I know people who are very liberal and who aren't racist, and yet they still have a hard time articulating exactly how and why policies that are inherently based on giving advantages to people of specific races are acceptable, when they've spent years hearing about how policies that give advantages to people because of their race are bad and terrible, when those people are white.<br /> <br /> There is obviously some natural tension there, and if you haven't had it broken down and explained in a logical and coherent way how these policies aren't racist, even if they are based on giving advantages to members of specific races over others, then some people will end up fairly confused by the whole idea, even absent any sort of misinformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T02:12:47-07:00","id":1088666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088644#post1088644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But fair or not, at the end of the day, if someone wants to implement Policy X, then it's ultimately on them to convince other people to go along with it since if they can't convince people to go along with it, then it's not going to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>But at this moment in time in the US, the fight is not (generally) over implementing new policies, but protecting existing policies or expanding them to cover more people.<br /> <br /> All the policies you were talking about already exist. They're already in place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But realistically they're not going to stop misinforming people anytime soon, so the only options are to either do a better job of getting the real message across in an understandable way, or simply give up and accept that the conservative misinformation is here to stay. </div> </div> </div>This excludes any efforts to influence conservatives that agree that the misinformation is bad to act against it even though it's acting against their political tribe.<br /> <br /> There are more actors in this than &quot;progressives,&quot; and, &quot;misinformation brokers.&quot; They have their share of civic responsibility towards allowing an honest contest of ideas in the public.<br /> <br /> And sure, the messaging hasn't been perfect, but it never is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T05:25:14-07:00","id":1088710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088644#post1088644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll agree it doesn't help when you have people undermine those sorts of policies, especially members of minorities like Thomas Sowell or Ben Carson or Michelle Malkin or whomever. But fair or not, at the end of the day, if someone wants to implement Policy X, then it's ultimately on them to convince other people to go along with it since if they can't convince people to go along with it, then it's not going to happen. Now it <i>is</i> very easy to point fingers at the conservative misinformation. But realistically they're not going to stop misinforming people anytime soon, so the only options are to either do a better job of getting the real message across in an understandable way, or simply give up and accept that the conservative misinformation is here to stay.<br /> <br /> That said, I think there has been a problem with relaying these kind of ideas, even absent conservative misinformation. I know people who are very liberal and who aren't racist, and yet they still have a hard time articulating exactly how and why policies that are inherently based on giving advantages to people of specific races are acceptable, when they've spent years hearing about how policies that give advantages to people because of their race are bad and terrible, when those people are white.<br /> <br /> There is obviously some natural tension there, and if you haven't had it broken down and explained in a logical and coherent way how these policies aren't racist, even if they are based on giving advantages to members of specific races over others, then some people will end up fairly confused by the whole idea, even absent any sort of misinformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point.<br /> <br /> Also, just passing, but I wanted to add that, as an European, the whole idea of white people don't have a culture of their own is just amusing me to no end, although I could see how it might be a problem in the US. That doesn't mean the US doesn't have a cultural heritage, because it's a hodgepodge thing ( every country is a hodgepodge of ethnicities, religions, phylosophies, etc.), it's just...very young and consist of a lot of the above mentioned. So, it could be a reason, why identity politics is so much prevalent over there, but I also think that what was going on now and the last several years is somewhat of a zeitgeist and it will change over time (or rather, it already does).<br /> <br /> However, I don't really agree that it's the reason why subcultures are came into being. A lot of them originated in countries with strong cultural identity and the most of them are everything but white-only groups and non-whites have subcultures of their own, although, I might say, in some cases and for some people being a non-white is already a subculture, yes.<br /> <br /> For answering the questions: yes, I'm white and no, I never felt the lack of cultural identity, although neither I defined myself through group identities, such as race, nation, even subculture. I have a definite inclination toward specific subcultures, but I never thought of myself as &quot;an XY&quot;. I even had arguments back in the day with classmates, who constantly wanted to put me in one or the other. Honestly, it's still a little weird to me how that group identity (and the making up of those groups and identities) is such a big part of other individuals' life, how important for them to say &quot;I'm an (insert identity/group)&quot;, but I guess I was always somewhat a loner, or at least rabidly individual in heart and soul. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not much surprise my first favorite Clan, as a teen in Masquerade was the Gangrel (that shifted since then, but I still like them).<br /> <br /> Ps: What was the problem exactly with the charging bull statue? To be honest, I never, ever heard about it before it came up here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-06-2017, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T10:58:31-07:00","id":1088799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088626#post1088626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For purposes of clarity, do you have some examples you can provide of that? Thank you regardless. ^.^</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://danieljmitchell.wordpress.com/2012/06/30/food-stamps-handouts-and-the-ever-expanding-welfare-state/\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>. Food stamps are a nice example, especially because the perception is that they only go to minorities who don't want to work. Really the only problem you should find searching for people railing against handouts is the fact that 'handouts' can refer to informational papers handed out by teachers and others. Romney, and then Jeb Bush, somewhat infamously made declarations directed at certain groups that, 'If you want free stuff vote for the other guy.' There's also been a long standing belief among the Republican party that minorities only vote Democrat for 'free stuff.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088633#post1088633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of white people honestly believe that racism is wrong - that treating one group of people worse than another group of people, because of their ethnicity or skin color is wrong and likewise, that treating one group of people better than another group of people because of their ethnicity or skin color, is also wrong. This is where you start running into issues with with &quot;reverse racism&quot; where groups begin passing things like racial quotas or what not, or colleges adding points to potential recruits based off of race and many white people say, &quot;Wait a second. Weren't you saying this was a problem when white people were doing it? So isn't it still a problem if other people are doing it?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this example is that in some places people weren't doing it consciously. They just tended to give, in this example, white people a better choice due to ingrained attitudes about things. One college might have someone in place who was actively racist, another just biased, and another entirely open minded. The end result was still less minorities going to colleges than should have been.<br /> <br /> If a recruiter is the type of person who needs to see a black person at 110% to be considered worthy, in their mind, to a white person at 50-100%, then points are the thing to help until we get less biased people in that job place.<br /> <br /> It's the type of thing that can be hard to fix, because a quota can be filled by reasonable applicants or by the first POC that comes in line, who may not be appropriate for the position. This can be done through laziness or malice. And the ruling will get the blame if Eleanor from Minnesota stamps a form 'Accepted' when she didn't bother to look beyond the response to the 'Race' category that would have made her throw it out before.<br /> <br /> Priority-wise it's about negating the effects of racism and balancing out the effects of biases until all people are treated equal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Clarified 'the effects of' 05-06-2017, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T10:59:19-07:00","id":1088800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088604#post1088604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be specific, when you are accustomed to the privilege of being able to look down on others. <br /> <br /> I can't think of any privileges I have that I would begrudge other people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see a lot of white people locally who get incredibly upset about minorities using the same welfare policies that they themselves take advantage of.<br /> <br /> The archetypal &quot;Welfare Queen&quot; are a tool to say that black people don't deserve welfare because they're just going to steal people's money. <br /> <br /> I'm sure a lot of white people would do a dramatic 180 on welfare if it became a white-only thing.<br /> <br /> I'll just cheerfully quote the Wikipedia article because I'm on my phone and can't do exhaustive checks:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Race is brought up constantly in policies as to categorize whether it is a Black or White issue and in welfare's history there's a switch in the way the public is educated through news media. Until early in the year of 1965, the news media was conveying only White [people] as living in poverty however that perception had changed to Black [people] Some of the influences in this shift could have been the civil rights movement and urban riots from the mid 60s. Welfare had then shifted from being a White issue to a Black issue and during this time frame the war on poverty had already begun. Subsequently, news media portrayed stereotypes of Black [people] as lazy, undeserving and welfare queens. These shifts in media don't necessarily establish the population living in poverty decreasing. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T20:00:52-07:00","id":1088970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088571#post1088571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bingo. A lot of white people are terrified of no longer being seen as the default or the majority and are somehow viewing that as discrimination... without realizing that this is how they've made <i>literally everyone else feel</i> forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they do, being the default is the only real &quot;culture&quot; that all american whites have, and it is really a non-culture. If they lose that th