o has lived in Georgia my entire life, THIS EXACTLY! The Bullhonkey Heritage not hate slogan is entirely based on that need for an identity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T23:03:52-07:00","id":1089014,"title":"","content":"I also think it's only natural for most people to take some kind of pride in their heritage and the history of their family and nation (or group that they identify with). And few people are terriblyproud when they're descended from a horrible person. So very often people will tend to &quot;dress up&quot; their ancestors or try to look at a more positive spin on things because they don't want to think that granddad or great-granddad was a monster, or at least supported a monstrous cause. <br /> <br /> So even when someone's ancestors did something terrible, people will often try to find ways to make them more sympathetic or heroic or try to avoid thinking too hard about the terrible things they did. I think that's just human nature, and it's something you'll see in pretty much every society in every part of the world. Groups that are completely honest and upfront about the flaws of their ancestors are fairly rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T12:51:48-07:00","id":1089322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1088463#post1088463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Plato, Mozart, Socrates, Ed Greenwood, Stephen Hawking, the Group of Seven, Leonardo Di Vinci, Micheal Angelo, entire genras of music like country/classical/polka/rock/heavy metal/punk music, the scientific method, the modern represental Democratic system like the Parliamentary system, the invention of countless new mediums for art such as movies, television, music recording devices, countless poets and so on is no culture?!?</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing to say is that this is a little constructed after the fact. Plato and Socrates would have in no sense seen themselves as &quot;white&quot;, but rather as Hellenes/Greek, vastly cultural distinct in their opinion to the barbarians in Croatia and Italy and absolutely not the same race (they even viewed themselves as quite distinct from those who spoke other Greek dialects). Similarly Michelangelo wouldn't have even seen himself as Italian, but as Tuscan and even faced racism in the rest of Italy on occasion for his foreign habits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:19:18-07:00","id":1089337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1089322#post1089322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to say is that this is a little constructed after the fact. Plato and Socrates would have in no sense seen themselves as &quot;white&quot;, but rather as Hellenes/Greek, vastly cultural distinct in their opinion to the barbarians in Croatia and Italy and absolutely not the same race (they even viewed themselves as quite distinct from those who spoke other Greek dialects). Similarly Michelangelo wouldn't have even seen himself as Italian, but as Tuscan and even faced racism in the rest of Italy on occasion for his foreign habits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but it's the same with every big group that was constructed lately. &quot;Black&quot;, or &quot;indigenous American&quot;, or Asian&quot; aren't more of an unified cultural heritage than &quot;white&quot; or &quot;European&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:03:06-07:00","id":1089367,"title":"","content":"You gotta think about context, there.<br /> <br /> One, that Black is used different ways depending on the context. It can mean two different things in the same context and in the same sentence, even. When we use it to talk about the Black experience in America, there is the potential for that to describe the experiences of African-Americans, or we might be talking about the experiences of people who are coded as Black in the United States or elsewhere, which is not a cultural heritage but is definitely a shared experience.<br /> <br /> Other people can also be describing the Black experience in their unique cultural context, though plenty of people who aren't African-American tend to be eager to distance themselves from the label. That's why West Indians insist they aren't black, or how you'll get Nigerians who refuse to be associated with Black people in the States.<br /> <br /> Most of what draws us together is a mixture of white people lumping everyone who is Black together in addition to the actual, shared experiences of being coded as Black by other people.<br /> <br /> It's complicated, but worth understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:31:01-07:00","id":1089384,"title":"","content":"Ok, I understand that these groups have shared cultural phenomenons, which are applicable to all the smaller groups to some extent, but that's also true for white people.<br /> <br /> My opinion is that saying &quot;black people have a shared identity due to their experiences as a minority (if I understood sufficiently what you wanted to say), but white people don't have a culture and identity, because everything which is connected to them are in fact only part of the smaller group's culture&quot; is just double standards, especially since there was always a constant exchange, spreading and sharing of ideas and cultural phenomenon (just take a look on the languages) in Europe and I guess in America too. Take the concept of knighthood and chivalry for example, it's not only French, or British, or German, it's European.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:50:06-07:00","id":1089395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1089337#post1089337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but it's the same with every big group that was constructed lately. &quot;Black&quot;, or &quot;indigenous American&quot;, or Asian&quot; aren't more of an unified cultural heritage than &quot;white&quot; or &quot;European&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing to remember about African-Americans is that they don't have the same sense of history about themselves that white Americans do. Most white Americans have an idea of what country their family originated from. Many know if their ancestors came from Germany, or Ireland, or France. Many white Americans last names reflect this heritage. In fact, if you meet someone on the street and they give you their last name, it's often possible to identity where someone's ancestors were from.<br /> <br /> But this isn't the case with African-Americans. Due to the way they were brought to the US, and to the way slave owners intentionally tried to stamp out knowledge of their origins, many blacks in the US don't know much more than the fact that their ancestors were from somewhere in Africa. While you could meet someone with the last name of Smith and the last name of Schneider, and know the first guy's ancestors came from England and the second guy's from Germany, there's no way for African-Americans do this. Their ancestors weren't even able to keep their own names. For most of them, there is no way to trace their ancestry back before the slave trade.<br /> <br /> So yes, &quot;Black&quot; is an artificial construct, but it is one constructed by white Americans in a deliberate attempt to erase the history of black slaves and prevent them from knowing where they came from or keeping their old traditions alive. Which means that blacks in the US have a sort of unified cultural heritage, in that unlike whites, or Hispanics, or Asians, or any other group, they <i>can't</i> have any other kind of cultural heritage, thanks to the impact of slavery.<br /> <br /> I'll also point out that indigenous Americans aren't the same. I've know a lot (in fact my brother's wife is a member of the Kalapuya) and they pretty much always identify themselves by their tribey much never call themselves &quot;native Americans&quot; or indigenous Americans except maybe when their in a technical position where they need to. The same is true for Asian-Americans. They'll call themselves Chinese-Americans, or Japanese-Americans, or Korean-Americans. The only time they tend to get called &quot;Asian-Americans&quot; is either when a white person does that, or they're filling out government forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:57:29-07:00","id":1089405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1089337#post1089337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but it's the same with every big group that was constructed lately. &quot;Black&quot;, or &quot;indigenous American&quot;, or Asian&quot; aren't more of an unified cultural heritage than &quot;white&quot; or &quot;European&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course (although noting what Leetsepeak said, i.e. Black and White might mean something unified in the US or certain contexts), what's your point?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take the concept of knighthood and chivalry for example, it's not only French, or British, or German, it's European. </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that's more a trait of Normanised cultures than European in general.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":". 05-07-2017, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T15:06:13-07:00","id":1089411,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> , that's quite interesting, thanks for writing it down, it helped to understand the situation and the argument better! However I think it means that the African-American shared identity was born in the US an thus, younger as it is and also it might be more tight and more homogenous in certain aspects than white American culture, but I don't think it means that white people doesn't have a shared cultural identity, aside from being the majority (as some posters said above) and it's certainly isn't the case in Europe. It just means that the white identity is broader and consist of a number of smaller identities, just like in the case of native Americans and individuals tend to identify themselves firstly by the smaller groups and then as a member of the larger group, if necessary. Like, I'm a Hungarian and then an European and then a white individual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T15:16:44-07:00","id":1089424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1089405#post1089405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course (although noting what Leetsepeak said, i.e. Black and White might mean something unified in the US or certain contexts), what's your point?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I answered that above? My main point was that I don't agree with the notion that black people have a shared cultural identity, while white people don't. It's just a bit differently organized and I acknowledged that &quot;blackness&quot; might be more of a foremost identity consideration for black people in the US, than &quot;whiteness&quot; for whites, but that doesn't mean they don't have a shared culture, it's just not revolving mainly around skin color, but other things. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd argue that's more a trait of Normanised cultures than European in general. </div> </div> </div>At first, sure, it's true, but we have knights and knighthoods, even literature in Hungary after a certain point and we were hardly Normanised. It originated there, sure, but it became an European cultural phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:05:51-07:00","id":1089443,"title":"","content":"Yes. Generally when we Americans say 'black culture,' and the we is referring to North Americans, we're talking about American black culture, which is different from Kenyan black culture, which is different from South African black culture and further from Afro-Brazilian culture.<br /> <br /> Just like when we say 'white people' or even 'white culture' we're not usually talking about Australians or white Slavic peoples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:36:00-07:00","id":1089462,"title":"","content":"To the chivalry point, chivalry as we understand it today is a modern construct. Real chivalry was a birthright of the nobility where you could rape and murder and still be considered chivalrous. Here is a medievalist from the US Naval Academy on the topic:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.usna.edu/Users/history/abels/hh381/Chivalry.htm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.usna.edu/CMS/_standard3.0/_files/img/logo.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.usna.edu/Users/history/abels/hh381/Chivalry.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Navigation Error :: USNA </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.usna.edu/Users/history/abels/hh381/Chivalry.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.usna.edu/Users/history/abels/hh381/Chivalry.htm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T17:47:30-07:00","id":1089489,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider is that a lot of american &quot;ethnic&quot; whites willingly shed most of their cultural heritage in the latter half of the last century in exchange for the WASPs approval. Sure there are a lot of Italian and Irish and German Americans, but how many of them (Especially among the younger generations that used geek cultures as a substitute for those identities) actually have a meaningful connection to that Irishness or Italianess or Germanicness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T17:49:18-07:00","id":1089491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1089424#post1089424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I answered that above? My main point was that I don't agree with the notion that black people have a shared cultural identity, while white people don't. It's just a bit differently organized and I acknowledged that &quot;blackness&quot; might be more of a foremost identity consideration for black people in the US, than &quot;whiteness&quot; for whites, but that doesn't mean they don't have a shared culture, it's just not revolving mainly around skin color, but other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>You did misunderstand me. African-American people have a shared cultural heritage. West-Indian people sometimes describe themselves as having a shared cultural heritage. People of African descent sometimes describe themselves as having a shared cultural heritage.<br /> <br /> What &quot;all Black people&quot; have in countries like the United States, or in European countries is not a shared cultural heritage, but a shared <i>experience </i>of being read, stereotyped and conceptualized as a monolithic concept of Black identity, which is comprised of stereotypes which in a given place may be constructed differently, but are all assigned on the basis of skin color.<br /> <br /> In the United States, you can be Nigerian or Jamaican or from any variety of places, and your black skin will lead people, especially non-black people, to conceptualize you and treat you in the same way that they treat an African-American whose ancestors were slaves in Virginia. That is not shared cultural heritage, but it is a shared experience of Blackness and how we are received.<br /> <br /> This exists simultaneously with the linked-fate and sense of cross-cultural affinity that develops as a <i>result </i>of Blackness being essentialized by non-black people. My family is from D.C. and I have absolutely no links to Africa that I can conceptualize, but my friends from Kenya, Ethiopia and Nigeria who I attended the institution with, we could all talk about the experience of being stereotyped and treated certain ways by non-black people on campus and in the world, because regardless of our individual heritage, those people would look at us and see us a singular Black identity and act accordingly. That common experience was a point of affinity and bonding for us.<br /> <br /> I don't think white people have that same experience on the basis of how their white skin is received, or at least, if that does happen, it is nowhere near the same degree that it occurs for Black people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 05-07-2017, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T09:33:54-07:00","id":1089830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1089491#post1089491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think white people have that same experience on the basis of how their white skin is received, or at least, if that does happen, it is nowhere near the same degree that it occurs for Black people.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are starting to see it though. There are quite a few places, especially on the internet, where white folk get together to commiserate over their treatment at the hands of minorities. It would almost be laughable if not for the fact that this tends to give those people an &quot;under siege&quot; mentality, where they feel victimized and constantly under attack by minorities. You're seeing the same thing with men, or straight people, or Christians, or other groups, which were previously in positions of absolute supremacy.<br /> <br /> So while a &quot;shared white experience&quot; didn't exist before, I think it's starting to take hold. And, to a degree, it's only natural. The Census Bureau suggests that by 2045 - in about one more generation, white Americans will no longer be the majority population in the US. White people will no longer be the &quot;norm&quot; against which everything else is measured.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the voices that are loudest in this process tend to be the ones who are the most racist and give a lot of white people the impression that they're under attack. Which is not really a good thing. Hopefully that will start to change in the long run, but who can tell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T12:08:55-07:00","id":1089875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1089424#post1089424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I answered that above? My main point was that I don't agree with the notion that black people have a shared cultural identity, while white people don't. It's just a bit differently organized and I acknowledged that &quot;blackness&quot; might be more of a foremost identity consideration for black people in the US, than &quot;whiteness&quot; for whites, but that doesn't mean they don't have a shared culture, it's just not revolving mainly around skin color, but other things.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, but I wasn't really claiming anything about a unified black culture or even mentioned black people at all. To follow your point though what are some of these elements of common white culture?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1089424#post1089424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At first, sure, it's true, but we have knights and knighthoods, even literature in Hungary after a certain point and we were hardly Normanised. It originated there, sure, but it became an European cultural phenomenon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again not in all countries, in Ireland we didn't have knights or chivalric literature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T13:35:16-07:00","id":1089931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are starting to see it though. There are quite a few places, especially on the internet, where white folk get together to commiserate over their treatment at the hands of minorities. It would almost be laughable if not for the fact that this tends to give those people an &quot;under siege&quot; mentality, where they feel victimized and constantly under attack by minorities. You're seeing the same thing with men, or straight people, or Christians, or other groups, which were previously in positions of absolute supremacy.<br /> <br /> So while a &quot;shared white experience&quot; didn't exist before, I think it's starting to take hold. And, to a degree, it's only natural. The Census Bureau suggests that by 2045 - in about one more generation, white Americans will no longer be the majority population in the US. White people will no longer be the &quot;norm&quot; against which everything else is measured.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the voices that are loudest in this process tend to be the ones who are the most racist and give a lot of white people the impression that they're under attack. Which is not really a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, I'm not &quot;white&quot; by your standards, in spite of the color of skin, because I'm latin american. However, I'm not &quot;unprivileged&quot; in my country (not that this accounts for a lot). Anycase, I cannot empathize with the &quot;white privilege&quot; because I know that US has a very complex issue with race that goes beyond skin color and cannot be easily compared with similar issues of my country.<br /> <br /> With &quot;man&quot; I can empathize better, because there's nearly universal privileges of woman that aren't a recent victory, but rather a survival of very old models that can be traced directly to the patriarchy: For instance, things like the fact that the woman will almost surely get to keep the child if the parents divorce (based on old assumptions of the role of woman as the one who babysits). It's easy to understand how this can be jarring for fathers in many situations, and it's directly related to what sociologists call &quot;gender issues&quot;. Too bad that the school of gender issues it's dominated by a movement that isn't going to care, hence the need of search support...in other places.<br /> <br /> You see, if you're &quot;privileged&quot;, but have a problem related to your privileged gender, skin color or whatever, you can't get the assistance of &quot;the system&quot; in regards to &quot;your privileges&quot;, because it's likely that if your situation wasn't subtly solved by your privileges in the first place, then it's outside of their scope (or worse, you're being injured by, let's say, &quot;negative privilege&quot;). So, if you have a problem, you need to go to the people that will hear you...which are not the major defenders of the &quot;socialy acceptable&quot;, that will reject your &quot;victim card&quot; in account of your &quot;privileges&quot;, but rather those who would question what's socialy acceptable...which, of course, will include immoral people like racists.<br /> <br /> Is my opinion that this is a great way of leftist movements to send water to the mills of the enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T14:43:06-07:00","id":1089973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1089931#post1089931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, I'm not &quot;white&quot; by your standards, in spite of the color of skin, because I'm latin american. However, I'm not &quot;unprivileged&quot; in my country (not that this accounts for a lot). Anycase, I cannot empathize with the &quot;white privilege&quot; because I know that US has a very complex issue with race that goes beyond skin color and cannot be easily compared with similar issues of my country.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part, the way America as a whole views race hasn't fundamentally changed since the 1600's. Most people are still operating along a 400 year old paradigm. While the US government (in the form of the Census) and colleges and a few other places have progressed, most individuals and private businesses have not.<br /> <br /> In many parts of the country there are basically 4 races. Black, White, Native American and Asian. When people don't fit into this, it can cause all sorts of confusion.<br /> <br /> For example, Hispanics aren't really a race, they're an ethnicity - being Hispanic means you (or your ancestors) came from an area that was under the Spanish empire (generally South and Central America along with parts of the Caribbean). And this means you can have black Hispanics, white Hispanics, indigenous Hispanics, asian Hispanics and all manner of mixes between them. This causes no end of consternation among people who think Hispanics are a race of people with brown skin.<br /> <br /> So in the US, sometimes Hispanics are considered white. And sometimes, they're not. It just depends on whose asking and what answers they offer. An ethnicity like that is a square peg that people are trying to make fit into a round hole, and it doesn't really mesh with the US' racial paradigm, but by golly if we won't figure out a way to shove it in there anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This can also cause other issues, like with people from the Middle East. If a form has, &quot;White, White (non-Hispanic), Black, Asian, Native American,&quot; what exactly do they fill out? White? Asian?If they're lucky there's a place to write in something, but that's not always the case.<br /> <br /> And of course, you have people who are of mixed race and they often get left out in the cold altogether.<br /> <br /> So basically how we look at race is very complicated, and it's largely defined by a system created hundreds of years ago, but nobody can agree how to go about updating or changing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-08-2017, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T08:04:39-07:00","id":1090312,"title":"","content":"By the way, I always found it strange that you have to select your &quot;race&quot; in american cuestionaries and documents. I never seen something like that in my country (Spain), only nationality. So anyone from the USA will be the same to us, maybe only making a distinction in the case of latin-americans due to our shared heritage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T08:15:23-07:00","id":1090319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1089973#post1089973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the most part, the way America as a whole views race hasn't fundamentally changed since the 1600's. Most people are still operating along a 400 year old paradigm. While the US government (in the form of the Census) and colleges and a few other places have progressed, most individuals and private businesses have not.<br /> <br /> In many parts of the country there are basically 4 races. Black, White, Native American and Asian. When people don't fit into this, it can cause all sorts of confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>White diversity used to be more widely recognized - not always in a good way. For example. during much of the 20th century, efforts have been made to suppress white immigrants coming from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immigration_Act_of_1924\" target=\"_blank\">Eastern Europe</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-Italianism\" target=\"_blank\">Italy</a>, and in the 1940's it became <a href=\"http://www.foitimes.com/gasummary.htm\" target=\"_blank\">very unpopular to be German</a>. If the sheer number of racist slurs for everyone who isn't of British ancestry wasn't a hint, there was plenty of hate and othering to go around for anyone at all not born in the USA, but <i>especially</i> people who were not white anglo-saxon protestants. It wasn't always about <a href=\"https://aleteia.org/2015/11/09/the-klan-and-the-catholics/\" target=\"_blank\">ethnicity</a>, either. Today, you can see it in conservative speakers who talk about how immigrants need to &quot;assimilate&quot; (as opposed to &quot;integrate&quot; or &quot;synthesize&quot;) into the existing culture, shedding whatever culture they had previously. <br /> <br /> If there is a feeling in the US today that &quot;white&quot; identity is formless, without definition... that may be partially self-inflicted. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T12:31:58-07:00","id":1090430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1090319#post1090319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> efforts have been made to suppress white immigrants coming from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immigration_Act_of_1924\" target=\"_blank\">Eastern Europe</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Cough...'Brexit'...cough...<br /> <br /> Seriously, my friends out there are quite concerned.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T12:45:48-07:00","id":1090440,"title":"","content":"Don't forget the contrast between black people in America and in Europe. In America the overwhelming majority of black people have ancestors who used to be slaves. The culture of their ancestors who lived in Africa was just about entirely erased, meaning that they became Americans with American culture. Contrast that with black people in Europe, where the overwhelming majority is of a 1st to 4th generation immigrant, many of whom still think fondly of their home countries and frequently visit them. In my country alone there are people Turkey, Morocco, Suriname, the Antilles and many other countries, not always with colonial roots. They consider themselves to be a mix of wherever they are from and the European country they live in, with people on both sides that lean more towards either option. This has caused some incidents now and then, most notably with the long arm of Sultan Erdogan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T13:34:49-07:00","id":1090461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the most part, the way America as a whole views race hasn't fundamentally changed since the 1600's. Most people are still operating along a 400 year old paradigm. While the US government (in the form of the Census) and colleges and a few other places have progressed, most individuals and private businesses have not.<br /> <br /> In many parts of the country there are basically 4 races. Black, White, Native American and Asian. When people don't fit into this, it can cause all sorts of confusion.<br /> <br /> For example, Hispanics aren't really a race, they're an ethnicity - being Hispanic means you (or your ancestors) came from an area that was under the Spanish empire (generally South and Central America along with parts of the Caribbean). And this means you can have black Hispanics, white Hispanics, indigenous Hispanics, asian Hispanics and all manner of mixes between them. This causes no end of consternation among people who think Hispanics are a race of people with brown skin.<br /> <br /> So in the US, sometimes Hispanics are considered white. And sometimes, they're not. It just depends on whose asking and what answers they offer. An ethnicity like that is a square peg that people are trying to make fit into a round hole, and it doesn't really mesh with the US' racial paradigm, but by golly if we won't figure out a way to shove it in there anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's very interesting...so I may or may not be white, my whiteness it's an undefined variable :P. Yea, I had some data on that.<br /> <br /> Once I heard from a racist post somewhere in the net that to be the whitest color of white you needed to be<i> a Protestant</i> (or that such was somehow an important part of &quot;white culture&quot;)...<br /> And I was like, WTF?, WTF has that to do with <i>race</i>!?...are such statements considered reasonable among some people there, or was just crazytalk?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, I always found it strange that you have to select your &quot;race&quot; in american cuestionaries and documents. I never seen something like that in my country (Spain), only nationality. So anyone from the USA will be the same to us, maybe only making a distinction in the case of latin-americans due to our shared heritage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither in mine (Argentina) as far as I know (I'm no expert)...which doesn't mean racism doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> Some people here hold prejudices against native americans. This prejudice it's rare among common people (no anty-native neigborhood + a LOT of people have indigenous blood, like, the majority), but it's very serious because it's usually pressent from very powerful and entrenched landlords (that still live like 400 years ago, they even have slaves in spite of this being against the law). Also, native american comunities recive very little love of the powers that be, making it the most serious racism problem in the country in my opinion...<br /> <br /> Some people think that the decendants of non spanish europeans and north americans are inherently better people than descendants from spaniards. This &quot;racism&quot; comes from the comunities of european immigrants (mostly from Itally and France) that make up a strong portion of the population.<br /> <br /> Asians aren't usually discriminated...but they do discriminate the rest of argentines :P (well, no, that isn't true. They do get to discriminate in some places, but mostly they don't)<br /> <br /> And a bout Black people...there sure isn't a lot of racism right now...but there was a LOT. And for real, not like todays naivete. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afro-Argentines\" target=\"_blank\">The history it's rather interesting</a>. Or if you want, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zjJc_5kfPjU\" target=\"_blank\">the short version</a><br /> <br /> Nowdays you're not going to be asked to declare your &quot;race&quot; in any official document (as far as I know), nor you will find organized groups of people willing to kick you from their neigborhood because of your race nor for your ethnicity (exept, maybe, in very remote towns). We don't have a complex &quot;race paradigm&quot;, nor comunities obsessed with racial purity. Howerver, in the big picture, I think the &quot;white people&quot; it's somewhat more privileged, and native americans have the worse deal. Racism exist but in a diferent shape, and perhaps, to a lesser degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-09-2017, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T15:05:44-07:00","id":1090494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1090461#post1090461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once I heard from a racist post somewhere in the net that to be the whitest color of white you needed to be<i> a Protestant</i> (or that such was somehow an important part of &quot;white culture&quot;)...<br /> And I was like, WTF?, WTF has that to do with <i>race</i>!?...are such statements considered reasonable among some people there, or was just crazytalk?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, that's just them being butthurt antinomianistic special snowflakes because their ancestors were charred black after being burnt at the stake for their heresy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T17:24:19-07:00","id":1090531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1090461#post1090461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's very interesting...so I may or may not be white, my whiteness it's an undefined variable :P. Yea, I had some data on that.<br /> <br /> Once I heard from a racist post somewhere in the net that to be the whitest color of white you needed to be<i> a Protestant</i> (or that such was somehow an important part of &quot;white culture&quot;)...<br /> And I was like, WTF?, WTF has that to do with <i>race</i>!?...are such statements considered reasonable among some people there, or was just crazytalk?</div> </div> </div> </div>It stems from cultural supremacism. I think that at some point after certain people of Northern European stock established that they were the pinnacle of civilisation, they asked themselves questions like &quot;Why is it that we're so awesome and the Irish aren't?&quot;. How do you answer questions like that? Science! Specifically biology. I mention the Irish, because I actually read a post somewhere claiming that there was a time when they didn't count as white. To be honest, I guessed that that was an idea that an Irish-American came up with to distance his identity from our old racist customs. But it turns out that there was at least one theory that they were more closely related to Cro-Magnons and by extension, Africans, than Anglo-Saxons, based upon morphological surveys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T23:10:15-07:00","id":1090602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1090531#post1090531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It stems from cultural supremacism. I think that at some point after certain people of Northern European stock established that they were the pinnacle of civilisation, they asked themselves questions like &quot;Why is it that we're so awesome and the Irish aren't?&quot;. How do you answer questions like that? Science! Specifically biology. I mention the Irish, because I actually read a post somewhere claiming that there was a time when they didn't count as white. To be honest, I guessed that that was an idea that an Irish-American came up with to distance his identity from our old racist customs. But it turns out that there was at least one theory that they were more closely related to Cro-Magnons and by extension, Africans, than Anglo-Saxons, based upon morphological surveys.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can find a lot of racist garbage from the Victorian era trying to argue that the Irish had &quot;negro&quot; skulls and thus weren't really white.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T23:29:49-07:00","id":1090605,"title":"","content":"Yeah, phrenology was some bullshit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T00:19:04-07:00","id":1090614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1053585-dear-white-people?p=1090531#post1090531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it turns out that there was at least one theory that they were more closely related to Cro-Magnons and by extension, Africans, than Anglo-Saxons, based upon morphological surveys.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was part of a larger belief that Celts (I.e. us, the highland Scots and the Welsh and until the 18th century the Cornish) were inherently incapable of self-governance as evidenced by our similarity to Africans, e.g. skull shape, affinity for music, etc<br /> Essentially too passionate to think rationally.<br /> <br /> That said, although my grandparents would have faced such racism from their landlord, it has no reality to modern Irish people and I most frequently encounter it used by Irish-Americans for the purpose you mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}